      "e2e",
      "daemon",
      "infrastructure"
    ],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-01-29T21:50:44.444Z",
    "started_at": "2026-01-29T22:51:20.910Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-01-29T23:14:12.765Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KG5VSSRD6430BCW8BM82TC0N",
        "created_at": "2026-01-29T21:50:55.245Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "## Scope\n\nFix the E2E test infrastructure so daemon fixtures load reliably. Currently:\n- Daemon starts with --kspec-dir pointing to temp fixtures\n- Returns empty data instead of YAML content\n- Causes 2+ minute timeouts in E2E tests\n\n## Related Observations\n- 01KFVPXS: E2E tests timeout after 2+ minutes\n- 01KFTGC4: E2E test verification blocked by daemon requirements\n- 01KFXVK5: dist/daemon/ can become stale without warning\n\n## Approach Options\n1. Debug ContextManager code paths for temp directory handling\n2. Add verbose/debug mode to daemon startup for diagnosis\n3. Create minimal reproduction case\n4. Check if dist/daemon staleness is root cause\n\n## Unblocks\n- @task-watcher-tests (P1) - AC-19 verification needs E2E\n- 01KFMMZW (P2) - API integration tests",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KG5Z8P3X5CQMGG9T3K6T1G99",
        "created_at": "2026-01-29T22:51:28.765Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Starting implementation of E2E reliability fixes:\n1. Health check polling - replacing fixed 2s wait with /api/health polling\n2. Daemon build staleness detection - warning when dist/daemon is older than source\n3. PidFileManager sync - copying file locking pattern from daemon to CLI version\n\nAlready completed: Health check polling in test-base.ts",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KG600TWW5QMR6QQ0RGCHMMFR",
        "created_at": "2026-01-29T23:04:40.093Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implementation complete. Changes made:\n\n1. **Health check polling** (test-base.ts:144-155)\n   - Replaced fixed 2s wait with /api/health endpoint polling\n   - 30 attempts at 100ms intervals (3s max)\n   - Clear error message on timeout\n\n2. **Daemon staleness detection** (serve.ts:32-61, 190-193)\n   - Added checkDaemonStaleness() function\n   - Recursively compares packages/daemon/src/ vs dist/daemon/ mtimes\n   - Shows warning before spawning daemon if source is newer\n\n3. **PidFileManager sync** (pid-utils.ts)\n   - Synced with daemon version to include file locking (ac-10b)\n   - Uses O_CREAT | O_EXCL for atomic file creation\n   - Inline retry pattern (no recursion) for stale file cleanup\n\nVerification:\n- npm test passes (69/71 tests, 2 pre-existing flaky tests)\n- daemon-pid.test.ts: 11/11 tests pass\n- E2E smoke tests: 5/5 pass\n- Staleness warning verified manually (touch + kspec serve start)",
        "supersedes": null
