  {
    "_ulid": "01KG6CJQVQ1SSF70RDKY8Y721R",
    "slugs": [
      "task-ralph-max-tasks-per-iteration-limiting"
    ],
    "title": "Implement: Ralph max-tasks-per-iteration limiting",
    "type": "task",
    "spec_ref": "@ralph-task-limit",
    "derivation": "auto",
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Implemented --max-tasks flag for ralph. PR #278 merged. Adds soft enforcement (wrap-up message) and hard enforcement (PreToolUse hook). Default is 1 task per iteration, 0 for unlimited.",
    "depends_on": [
      "@task-ralph-command-automated-task-loop"
    ],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 3,
    "tags": [],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-01-30T02:44:09.719Z",
    "started_at": "2026-01-30T02:44:46.050Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-01-30T04:03:21.903Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KG6CJQVPY003VNGCB5VDFMJM",
        "created_at": "2026-01-30T02:44:09.719Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implementation notes (auto-generated from spec):\n\nLimits how many tasks can be completed per iteration via --max-tasks flag. Default is 1 (conservative), 0 means unlimited. Enforcement is soft (message injection) then hard (PreToolUse hook blocking task start). Counts only kspec task complete commands (not submit, which is status change to pending_review).\n\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n- ac-flag: Given User runs kspec ralph, when --max-tasks flag is provided or defaults, then Parses N as positive integer (1-999) or 0 for unlimited; default is 1; invalid values exit with code 2\n- ac-detection: Given Agent completes a task (kspec task complete), when ACP update handler receives Bash tool call containing kspec task complete, then Ralph queries kspec for actual completion count since iteration start, not relying on pattern alone\n- ac-wrapup: Given N tasks completed this iteration (N equals max-tasks), when Detection triggers and count verified via kspec query, then Ralph writes marker file and injects wrap-up message telling agent to stop starting new tasks\n- ac-unlimited: Given --max-tasks 0 is specified, when Ralph runs iteration, then No task limit enforced (legacy behavior); no marker file written\n- ac-hook-block: Given Marker file exists at .claude/ralph-task-limit.json with active:true, when PreToolUse hook intercepts kspec task start command, then Hook blocks with message explaining task limit reached; allows other commands\n- ac-reset: Given New iteration begins, when Ralph starts iteration loop, then Counter resets to 0; stale marker files older than 1 hour are cleared\n- ac-marker-format: Given Task limit reached, when Marker file written, then File is JSON with active, since (ISO8601), max, completed, sessionId fields\n- ac-dryrun: Given --dry-run flag provided with --max-tasks N, when Ralph shows config, then Displays max-tasks configuration in dry-run output",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KG6CKME157948WER70QE8RHN",
        "created_at": "2026-01-30T02:44:38.977Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "## Implementation Context\n\n### Purpose\nAdd --max-tasks N flag to ralph that limits how many tasks can be completed per iteration. This prevents runaway automation and gives humans control over batch sizes.\n\n### Files to Modify\n\n1. **src/cli/commands/ralph.ts** - Core logic\n   - Add CLI option after line 598: .option('--max-tasks <n>', 'Max tasks per iteration (0 = unlimited)', '1')\n   - Track tasksCompletedThisIteration counter (reset at iteration start)\n   - Add detection in ACP update handler (around line 817-834) - pattern match 'kspec task complete' in Bash tool calls\n   - On detection: query kspec for actual completion count since iteration start\n   - If count >= maxTasks: write marker file, inject wrap-up message\n   - Clear marker file at iteration end\n\n2. **src/cli/commands/session.ts** - Stats query\n   - Add getIterationStats(ctx, since) function\n   - Returns { tasks_completed, tasks_started, completed_refs }\n   - Uses loadAllTasks() and filters by completed_at >= since\n\n3. **.claude/hooks/ralph-task-limit-guard.sh** - New hook\n   - Pattern follows existing kspec-worktree-guard.sh\n   - Intercepts 'kspec task start' commands\n   - Checks for marker file at .claude/ralph-task-limit.json\n   - If marker exists and active:true, block with explanatory message\n   - Otherwise allow\n\n4. **.claude/settings.json** - Register hook\n   - Add to existing PreToolUse[0].hooks array:\n   { 'type': 'command', 'command': '.claude/hooks/ralph-task-limit-guard.sh' }\n\n### Marker File Format (.claude/ralph-task-limit.json)\n{\n  'active': true,\n  'since': 'ISO8601 timestamp',\n  'max': 2,\n  'completed': 2,\n  'sessionId': 'ralph session ULID'\n}\n\n### Key Implementation Details\n\n**Detection Flow:**\n1. ACP update handler sees Bash tool call\n2. Pattern match 'kspec task complete' (not submit - submit just changes status to pending_review)\n3. Query kspec for completions since iteration start\n4. If threshold reached: write marker, inject message\n\n**Soft Enforcement (message injection):**\n- Use agent.client.prompt() to send a follow-up message\n- Message: 'Task limit reached (N tasks completed). Wrap up current work and exit cleanly. Do not start new tasks.'\n\n**Hard Enforcement (hook):**\n- PreToolUse hook blocks 'kspec task start'\n- Provides clear error message explaining limit\n- Agent can still run other commands\n\n**Stale Marker Protection:**\n- At iteration start, if marker exists and is > 1 hour old, delete it\n- Prevents stale markers from blocking future runs\n\n### Edge Cases\n- --max-tasks 0: Unlimited (legacy behavior)\n- kspec query failure: Log warning, don't crash iteration\n- Multiple ralph instances: Marker in project root means conflict possible - document this\n\n### Test Files to Create\n\n1. tests/ralph/task-limit.test.ts - Unit tests\n   - detectTaskCommand() pattern matching\n   - checkTaskCompletionCount() with time filtering\n   - Marker file operations (write/read/clear)\n   - getIterationStats() function\n\n2. tests/cli/ralph-task-limit.test.ts - CLI tests\n   - Flag parsing (valid, invalid, default)\n   - Dry-run shows max-tasks config\n\n3. tests/hooks/ralph-task-limit-guard.test.ts - Hook tests\n   - Allows when no marker\n   - Blocks when marker exists\n   - Ignores stale markers",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KG6DAX3AZAK5S1NTSQDP39BP",
        "created_at": "2026-01-30T02:57:21.515Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "## Implementation Complete\n\n### Files Modified\n1. **src/cli/commands/ralph.ts** - Core logic\n   - Added --max-tasks <n> CLI option (default 1, 0=unlimited)\n   - Added flag validation (0-999 range)\n   - Added info message with max-tasks configuration\n   - Added dry-run output showing max-tasks\n   - Added task limit marker file operations (write/read/clear/clearStale)\n   - Added extractBashCommand() to detect Bash tool calls from SessionUpdate\n   - Added detectTaskCompleteCommand() pattern matcher\n   - Added task completion detection in ACP update handler\n   - Added wrap-up message injection when limit reached\n   - Added marker file cleanup in finally block\n\n2. **src/cli/commands/session.ts** - Stats query\n   - Added IterationStats interface\n   - Added getIterationStats(ctx, since) function for querying completions\n\n3. **.claude/hooks/ralph-task-limit-guard.sh** - New PreToolUse hook\n   - Intercepts kspec task start commands\n   - Checks marker file at .claude/ralph-task-limit.json\n   - Blocks when marker exists with active:true\n   - Provides helpful error message with limit info\n\n4. **.claude/settings.json** - Hook registration\n   - Added ralph-task-limit-guard.sh to PreToolUse hooks array\n\n### Tests Added\n- tests/ralph/task-limit.test.ts (11 tests)\n- tests/hooks/ralph-task-limit-guard.test.ts (9 tests)\n- tests/cli/session-iteration-stats.test.ts (3 tests)\n\nAll 23 new tests pass. Existing tests unaffected.",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
