      {
        "_ulid": "01KG8N2K99ZCNTMQC8HB497JB3",
        "created_at": "2026-01-30T23:51:06.793Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Design decision: Implementing as 'kspec ralph end-iteration' CLI command. Agent invokes the command, ralph detects it via command monitoring (same pattern as task-limit detection), then gracefully ends the iteration after current prompt completes. File-based approach was considered but CLI is more consistent with other agent actions and provides better audit trail.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KG8NEAM04PVJ57E2AFR07B5R",
        "created_at": "2026-01-30T23:57:31.137Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implementation complete:\n\n1. Added EndIterationMarker interface and helpers (write/read/clear/clearStale)\n2. Added 'kspec ralph end-iteration' subcommand with --reason flag\n3. Modified ralph to detect end-iteration command via extractBashCommand pattern matching\n4. Added endIterationRequested state variable that triggers graceful loop exit after iteration\n5. Added cleanup in iteration start and session end to clear stale markers\n\nThe pattern follows the existing task-limit marker approach for consistency. Detection happens in the streaming update handler, and graceful exit occurs after the current iteration's reflect phase completes.\n\nTests added: tests/ralph/end-iteration.test.ts (8 tests, all passing)",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "automation": "eligible",
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
