    "title": "Design: Batch command execution via JSON",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "Batch command execution via JSON - Generic kspec batch command that accepts JSON array of CLI commands with args. Example: [{\"cmd\": \"item ac add\", \"ref\": \"@spec-1\", \"given\": \"...\", ...}]. Separates concerns: skills/scripts generate the JSON (smart translation), CLI executes it (dumb executor). Supports --dry-run for preview, --file or stdin input. Replaces need for command-specific bulk variants. Pairs with skills that translate intent (plan sections, templates) into batch JSON.",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
