    "description": "Check acceptance criteria for field references (item.field, status.field, etc.) that don't exist in the actual schema. Catches drift between spec prose and implementation reality.\n\nResearch findings from @01KFBDQE:\n- ACs reference 'children' but SpecItem has no children field (hierarchy is parse-time only)\n- ACs reference 'spec_ref.children' but spec_ref is just a string\n- ACs describe cascade operations that aren't schema-queryable\n\nImplementation approach:\n- Add checkACSchemaReferences() function similar to checkStaleness()\n- Extract field patterns from AC then clauses\n- Validate against SpecItem/Task schema fields\n- Add --drift flag to validate command\n- Report CompletenessWarning with type 'ac_schema_field_mismatch'",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #362. Added AC schema drift detection with checkACSchemaReferences() function that extracts field patterns from AC clauses and validates against SpecItem/Task schemas. Detects conceptual fields (children, parent) and ref strings incorrectly treated as objects. Added --drift flag to validate command. Includes 8 tests covering various drift scenarios.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 3,
    "tags": [],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-03T05:29:09.292Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-14T09:06:44.208Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-14T09:23:44.756Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGKCQ9WVQVT7BTW1TB3Y0J6R",
        "created_at": "2026-02-04T03:56:46.875Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Automation status set to needs_review: Task lacks description/notes - unclear what 'drift' refers to; needs clarification before spec'ing",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHDPW293AV70B36GWSHH36GY",
        "created_at": "2026-02-14T09:14:23.907Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implemented AC schema drift detection with:\n- checkACSchemaReferences() function that extracts field patterns from AC given/when/then clauses\n- Validates against actual SpecItem and Task schema fields\n- Detects conceptual fields like 'children' and 'parent' that exist at parse-time but aren't queryable\n- Detects refs like 'spec_ref.field' where spec_ref is actually a string, not an object\n- Added --drift flag to validate command\n- File extension filtering to avoid false positives (spec.yaml, task.json, etc.)\n- 8 tests covering: invalid fields, ref strings, valid fields, status fields, flag presence, exit codes, multiple drift issues",
