  {
    "_ulid": "01KGHFM9HW9KTCZC8XTYDV09YD",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Create zero-dependency bootstrap script for agent sessions",
    "type": "task",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #300 - 36565a76",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 1,
    "tags": [
      "cli",
      "dx",
      "bootstrap",
      "agent-first"
    ],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-03T10:09:05.084Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-03T10:09:53.426Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-04T09:06:01.942Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGHFNC9TZBNJ0BX2PCN9G4B4",
        "created_at": "2026-02-03T10:09:40.667Z",
        "author": "Claude",
        "content": "## Problem\n\nWhen an agent starts a session on a fresh clone or machine, kspec may not be built/linked/initialized. The agent then has to:\n1. Run npm install\n2. Run npm run build  \n3. Run npm link\n4. Run kspec init (which prompts interactively)\n5. Run kspec session start\n\nThis creates friction and the agent may not know the correct sequence.\n\n## Solution\n\nCreate a zero-dependency Node.js bootstrap script at `scripts/bootstrap.js` that:\n\n1. **Runs without npm install** - Uses only Node.js built-ins (child_process, fs, path)\n2. **Detects current state** - Checks if kspec is already working\n3. **Does minimal work** - Only runs steps that are needed\n4. **Is transparent** - Reports exactly what it did to the agent\n5. **Outputs session context** - Ends with session start info\n\n## Detection Logic\n\n1. Check if `kspec --version` works (command exists and runs)\n2. Check if `.kspec/` directory exists and is healthy\n3. If both pass, just run session start\n4. Otherwise, run the setup steps needed\n\n## Setup Steps (when needed)\n\n1. `npm install` - if node_modules missing or stale\n2. `npm run build` - if dist/ missing or stale  \n3. `npm link` - if kspec command not found\n4. `kspec init --no-prompt` - if .kspec/ not initialized\n5. `kspec session start` - always at the end\n\n## Output Format\n\nScript should output structured info for the agent:\n```\n=== Kspec Bootstrap ===\nStatus: [fresh_setup | already_configured | repaired]\n\nActions taken:\n- Installed dependencies (npm install)\n- Built project (npm run build)\n- Linked CLI (npm link)\n- Initialized shadow branch (kspec init)\n\n[session start output here]\n```\n\n## Location & Invocation\n\n- File: `scripts/bootstrap.js`\n- Run: `node scripts/bootstrap.js`\n- Add npm script: `\"bootstrap\": \"node scripts/bootstrap.js\"`\n\n## Documentation Updates\n\n1. Add to AGENTS.md - new section on session bootstrap\n2. Update INSTALL.md - mention bootstrap as alternative to manual steps\n3. Update CLAUDE.md - instruct agents to run bootstrap first",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGHGB5WEWYR4JHPY7DP49CC4",
        "created_at": "2026-02-03T10:21:34.990Z",
        "author": "Claude",
        "content": "Implementation complete:\n\nCREATED:\n- scripts/bootstrap.cjs - Zero-dependency Node.js script\n  - Uses CommonJS (.cjs) to work regardless of package.json type\n  - Detects: kspec CLI, .kspec/ dir, node_modules, dist/\n  - Only runs steps that are needed\n  - Reports actions taken with colored output\n  - Ends with session start output\n\nUPDATED:\n- package.json - Added \"bootstrap\" npm script\n- CLAUDE.md - Added bootstrap as first step in Quick Start\n- AGENTS.md - Updated 'For New Contributors' and 'Starting a Session' sections\n- INSTALL.md - Added bootstrap option in 'From Source' section\n\nTESTED:\n- Verified bootstrap detects already-configured state (skips setup)\n- Verified npm run bootstrap works\n- Existing tests have unrelated timeout failures (not introduced by this change)",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
  },
  {
    "_ulid": "01KGJ5DMRTSEWKEGAKCSS0DQKW",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Document loop mode blocking pattern to prevent premature end-iteration",
    "type": "task",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Documentation updates merged in PR #302. Added blocking vs end-iteration guidance to task-work skill, AGENTS.md, and kspec skill.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 2,
    "tags": [
      "documentation",
      "ralph",
      "loop-mode",
      "reflection"
    ],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-03T16:29:55.855Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-04T02:03:09.679Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-04T02:25:27.391Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGJ5ECYHJ59ZNMC7XTKSVZQ4",
        "created_at": "2026-02-03T16:30:20.626Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "## Problem\n\nIn Ralph session 01KGHBQ9WYVVK3PWNS55B8N108, the agent prematurely ended the loop after 2 iterations (of 10) by calling:\n\n```\nkspec ralph end-iteration --reason \"Task 01KGGTR7 requires architectural decisions beyond automation scope. Investigation complete, documented findings.\"\n```\n\nThe CORRECT behavior should have been:\n1. Mark task @01KGGTR7 as blocked with reason\n2. Mark automation status as needs_review\n3. Check `kspec tasks ready --eligible` for other work\n4. Continue the loop with remaining tasks\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe documentation teaches what NOT to do but doesn't explain what TO do instead. The agent saw:\n- \"Task seems complex is NOT an exit condition\" (task-work SKILL.md:335)\n- \"You can signal: kspec ralph end-iteration\" (task-work SKILL.md:327)\n\nBut there was no guidance saying: \"Block the task and continue to other work\"\n\n## Files Requiring Updates\n\n### 1. .claude/skills/task-work/SKILL.md\n\n**Section: Exit Conditions (lines 316-320)**\nCurrent text only mentions \"no eligible tasks\" - needs to clarify:\n- Check `kspec tasks ready --eligible` for OTHER tasks\n- Only end-iteration when ALL eligible tasks are blocked/done\n- One blocked task is not \"no eligible tasks\"\n\n**Section: What Is NOT an Exit Condition (lines 332-348)**\nTells agents what NOT to do but missing what TO do:\n- Add escalation pattern: try → block → continue → end-iteration\n- Explicitly state: \"Never use end-iteration just because ONE task is complex\"\n\n**Section: Explicit Loop End Signal (lines 322-330)**\nVague wording \"completed your focused work\" - needs tightening:\n- Valid: all eligible tasks blocked/completed\n- Invalid: one task is hard so I'm done\n\n**NEW SECTION NEEDED: Blocking vs End-Iteration**\nAdd table comparing three mechanisms:\n| Situation | Action | When to Use |\n|-----------|--------|-------------|\n| Task requires other task first | `kspec task block` | True dependency |\n| Task needs external input | `kspec task block` | Human decision needed |\n| Task is complex/hard | DO THE WORK | Always - complexity is not a blocker |\n| No more work possible | `kspec ralph end-iteration` | ALL tasks blocked/done |\n\n### 2. AGENTS.md\n\n**NEW SECTION: Using Task Blocking in Loop Mode (after line 234)**\nAdd guidance with examples:\n\n```bash\n# Pattern: When you discover a genuine blocker\nkspec task block @complex-task --reason \"Requires architectural decision on X\"\nkspec task set @complex-task --automation needs_review\nkspec tasks ready --eligible  # Check for other work\n# Continue with unblocked tasks\n```\n\nValid blocking reasons:\n- External dependency (API spec needed)\n- Human architectural decision required\n- Spec gap blocking understanding\n\nInvalid blocking reasons (DO THE WORK):\n- Task seems complex\n- Multiple test failures\n- Service needs to be running\n\n### 3. .claude/skills/kspec/SKILL.md (minor)\nCross-reference the new loop mode blocking guidance from task-work skill.\n\n## Key Message to Encode\n\nThe loop should ONLY end when:\n1. All automation-eligible tasks are completed, OR\n2. All remaining eligible tasks are blocked AND no unblocked work exists\n\nOne hard task should result in:\n1. Block that task with reason\n2. Mark as needs_review\n3. Move to next eligible task\n4. Loop continues\n\n## Session Evidence\n\nSession: 01KGHBQ9WYVVK3PWNS55B8N108\n- seq 2710: Agent added task note documenting investigation\n- seq 2714: Agent called end-iteration (WRONG)\n- Should have: blocked task, continued to @01KGGWAE (comma-separated tags task)",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGK69CXAW00RZN2G31C93VK4",
        "created_at": "2026-02-04T02:04:19.755Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Updated documentation in three files to clarify loop mode blocking pattern:\n\n1. **task-work/SKILL.md**: \n   - Rewrote Exit Conditions to emphasize 'no eligible tasks' means ALL tasks\n   - Added 'Blocking vs End-Iteration' section with comparison table\n   - Clarified that tasks must be ATTEMPTED before blocking\n   - Added valid/invalid end-iteration reasons\n   - Expanded 'What Is NOT an Exit Condition' with explicit guidance on what to do instead\n\n2. **AGENTS.md**:\n   - Added 'Task Blocking in Loop Mode' section after Task States\n   - Documents the attempt→block→check→continue pattern\n   - Lists valid vs invalid blocking reasons\n   - Example commands for proper blocking workflow\n\n3. **kspec/SKILL.md**:\n   - Added cross-reference note in Blocking section pointing to /task-work for loop mode details",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
  },
