  {
    "_ulid": "01KGP2PPFRPESKDEG850M2F784",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Fix doubled [REVIEW SUBAGENT] prefix in newSection output",
    "type": "task",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Fixed doubled prefix in createPrefixedRenderer: removed prefix from console.log wrapper (stdout.write handles it) and from newSection label argument. Added two tests.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 1,
    "tags": [],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-05T04:59:24.536Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-05T04:59:29.510Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-05T05:09:05.283Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGP37JYA2NTWB3XCPCNBZ7AP",
        "created_at": "2026-02-05T05:08:37.962Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Fixed doubled [REVIEW SUBAGENT] prefix in ralph loop output.\n\nRoot cause: createPrefixedRenderer in cli-renderer.ts had two independent sources of prefix doubling:\n\n1. withPrefixedOutput() wrapped both console.log and process.stdout.write to add the prefix. Since console.log output flows through stdout.write, the prefix was applied twice for any console.log-based output (headers, section labels, tool updates, etc.).\n\n2. newSection() manually prepended the prefix to the label (${prefix} ${label}) before passing it to inner.newSection(), which then got prefixed again by the wrappers.\n\nFix:\n- Removed prefix from console.log wrapper (line 295) - let stdout.write be the single source of prefixing\n- Removed manual prefix from newSection label (line 343) - pass just the label\n\nAdded tests verifying no double-prefixing for both console.log and stdout.write paths.",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
  },
  {
    "_ulid": "01KGR05MRK1VGWHX7CTHW64KDR",
    "slugs": [
      "implement-batch-command-execution"
    ],
    "title": "Implement Batch Command Execution",
    "type": "task",
    "spec_ref": "@batch-exec",
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #324. Implemented kspec batch with atomic (default) and immediate (--no-atomic) execution modes. 40 tests, 22 spec ACs. Addressed review feedback from both Codex and Claude CI: positional arg ordering, copy-back safety, finally-block cleanup, validation count accuracy.",
    "depends_on": [
      "@implement-batch-command-schema",
      "@implement-batch-allowed-commands"
    ],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 3,
    "tags": [],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-05T22:53:37.427Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-06T18:52:28.077Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-06T21:52:55.842Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGR05MRKC2P7MADTHFGB747E",
        "created_at": "2026-02-05T22:53:37.427Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implementation notes from plan:\n\nArchitecture builds on existing infrastructure:\n\n1. **Command registry** — Extend `src/cli/introspection.ts` to produce a map of command paths to their handler functions and metadata, including a `mutating: boolean` annotation. This enables dynamic dispatch without Commander.js parsing overhead and drives the allow/deny classification.\n\n2. **Batch executor** (`src/cli/batch-exec.ts`) — New module:\n   - `parseBatchInput(source)` — Reads from stdin/file/inline, parses JSON array\n   - `validateBatch(commands, registry, context)` — Pre-validates all commands: known command, required args, ref resolution (including forward refs from earlier commands in batch)\n   - `executeBatch(commands, registry, context, options)` — Executes validated commands sequentially, collects results, handles stop-on-error vs continue\n\n3. **Shadow commit batching** — Use a `context.batchMode` flag. When set, `commitIfShadow()` skips the commit. The batch executor issues a single commit after all operations complete (or after partial completion with `--continue`). The flag is set before execution and cleared after.\n\n4. **Forward reference resolution** — During pre-validation, track slugs that will be created by earlier commands. Build a \"planned refs\" set that the validator checks against when a ref doesn't exist yet. Only tracks creates, not deletes (documented limitation).\n\n5. **Confirmation suppression** — When `context.batchMode` is set, commands that check for `@trait-confirmation-prompt` behavior skip the prompt and proceed as if `--force` were passed.\n\n6. **Handler extraction** — Each command's `.action()` handler needs to be callable programmatically (not just via Commander.js parsing). Extract the core logic into importable functions that batch can call directly. Many commands already follow this pattern (e.g., `resolveTaskRefForBatch()`).\n\n7. **Test approach** — Unit tests for parse/validate/execute phases. Integration test with a temp kspec project running a real batch payload end-to-end. Test the full matrix: stdin/file/inline × stop-on-error/continue × success/failure/partial."
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGR1880314CP5YJAABQNX3MB",
        "created_at": "2026-02-05T23:12:31.235Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Scope: This is the main feature task. Responsible for the batch command itself (src/cli/commands/batch.ts), the batch executor module (src/cli/batch-exec.ts), shadow commit batching (context.batchMode flag), forward reference resolution, confirmation suppression, and the kspec batch CLI registration. Covers ACs: ac-stdin, ac-file, ac-inline, ac-stop-on-error, ac-continue, ac-prevalidate, ac-dry-run, ac-forward-ref, ac-single-commit, ac-partial-commit, ac-confirmation-suppressed, ac-invalid-json, ac-empty-batch. Depends on the other two tasks being done first or simultaneously — the command schema defines the input format and the allowed commands list drives validation.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGT5Q54EF33YJ9WCF374MJEB",
        "created_at": "2026-02-06T19:09:02.990Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implementation complete: batch command execution with two modes.\n\n**Atomic mode** (default): copies .kspec/ to temp dir, executes against copy, rolls back on failure, copies back + single shadow commit on success. Uses KSPEC_SPEC_DIR env var override in initContext() and setBatchMode() to suppress per-command shadow commits.\n\n**Immediate mode** (--no-atomic): executes against real .kspec/ state, per-command auto-commits via existing shadow machinery. No rollback on failure. --continue flag implies immediate mode.\n\nKey implementation details:\n- KSPEC_SPEC_DIR env var in initContext() for temp dir redirection\n- BatchExitError + exit interceptor to catch process.exit() calls\n- OutputCapture to intercept console.log/error/warn per command\n- resetCommandTree() to clear Commander state between dispatches\n- Auto-append --force for confirmation suppression\n- Strip ANSI via chalk.level=0 during dispatch\n- .git removed from temp copy to prevent worktree pointer leaks\n- Copy-back handles deletions by clearing real specDir first\n\nFiles created: batch-context.ts, commands/batch.ts\nFiles modified: batch-exec.ts, schema/batch.ts, parser/yaml.ts, parser/shadow.ts, cli/index.ts, commands/index.ts\nTests: 39 tests (21 unit + 18 integration), all passing\nFull test suite: 1823/1824 pass (1 pre-existing bun compilation failure)",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
  },
  {
    "_ulid": "01KGR05N2YJQSJM5J48YHGQP2J",
    "slugs": [
      "implement-batch-command-schema"
    ],
    "title": "Implement Batch Command Schema",
    "type": "task",
    "spec_ref": "@batch-command-schema",
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #321. Implemented batch command schema (Zod schemas for BatchCommand and BatchInput), parsing layer (stdin/file/inline with BatchParseError), and validation (command path resolution, arg mapping with kebab/camelCase, unknown command suggestions via fuzzy matching, missing required arg detection, commandFilter extension point). All 5 ACs covered by 40 unit tests. No regressions.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 3,
    "tags": [],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-05T22:53:37.758Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-06T08:23:55.728Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-06T09:03:26.862Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGR05N2Y7XEPBV0X7Y4SHGB7",
        "created_at": "2026-02-05T22:53:37.758Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implementation notes from plan:\n\nArchitecture builds on existing infrastructure:\n\n1. **Command registry** — Extend `src/cli/introspection.ts` to produce a map of command paths to their handler functions and metadata, including a `mutating: boolean` annotation. This enables dynamic dispatch without Commander.js parsing overhead and drives the allow/deny classification.\n\n2. **Batch executor** (`src/cli/batch-exec.ts`) — New module:\n   - `parseBatchInput(source)` — Reads from stdin/file/inline, parses JSON array\n   - `validateBatch(commands, registry, context)` — Pre-validates all commands: known command, required args, ref resolution (including forward refs from earlier commands in batch)\n   - `executeBatch(commands, registry, context, options)` — Executes validated commands sequentially, collects results, handles stop-on-error vs continue\n\n3. **Shadow commit batching** — Use a `context.batchMode` flag. When set, `commitIfShadow()` skips the commit. The batch executor issues a single commit after all operations complete (or after partial completion with `--continue`). The flag is set before execution and cleared after.\n\n4. **Forward reference resolution** — During pre-validation, track slugs that will be created by earlier commands. Build a \"planned refs\" set that the validator checks against when a ref doesn't exist yet. Only tracks creates, not deletes (documented limitation).\n\n5. **Confirmation suppression** — When `context.batchMode` is set, commands that check for `@trait-confirmation-prompt` behavior skip the prompt and proceed as if `--force` were passed.\n\n6. **Handler extraction** — Each command's `.action()` handler needs to be callable programmatically (not just via Commander.js parsing). Extract the core logic into importable functions that batch can call directly. Many commands already follow this pattern (e.g., `resolveTaskRefForBatch()`).\n\n7. **Test approach** — Unit tests for parse/validate/execute phases. Integration test with a temp kspec project running a real batch payload end-to-end. Test the full matrix: stdin/file/inline × stop-on-error/continue × success/failure/partial."
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGR18ASFFTFPT7ZW82GMT94E",
        "created_at": "2026-02-05T23:12:34.095Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Scope: Define and validate the batch command input schema. Responsible for the Zod schema for command objects ({command, args, id?}), arg-to-CLI-parameter mapping logic, and validation error messages (unknown command suggestions, missing required arg identification). This is the parseBatchInput and the schema portion of validateBatch. Covers ACs: ac-command-field, ac-args-mapping, ac-unknown-command, ac-missing-required, ac-id-field.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGS2C9RZC5MYSH2YR2BRTCJF",
        "created_at": "2026-02-06T08:51:27.135Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implemented batch command schema and validation:\n\nFiles created:\n- src/schema/batch.ts — Zod schemas (BatchCommandSchema, BatchInputSchema) and result types (BatchCommandResult, BatchExecSummary, BatchExecResult)\n- src/cli/batch-exec.ts — parseBatchInput() (stdin/file/inline), validateBatchCommands() with commandFilter extension point, reportBatchValidationErrors() (human + JSON)\n- tests/batch-schema.test.ts — 40 tests covering all 5 ACs + parse error paths\n\nFiles modified:\n- src/schema/index.ts — added batch re-export\n- src/cli/introspection.ts — added mandatory field to OptionMeta (distinguishes 'option must be provided' from 'value required when used')\n\nKey design decisions:\n- Uses existing introspection infrastructure (extractCommandTree, findCommand, flattenCommandTree) and suggest.ts (findClosestCommand) for command resolution and fuzzy suggestions\n- commandFilter option on validateBatchCommands() is the extension point for @01KGR05NE (allowed-commands task)\n- Supports both kebab-case and camelCase arg names via normalization\n- BatchParseError preserves JSON.parse position info for debugging",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
  },
