        "content": "Implementation notes from plan:\n\nArchitecture builds on existing infrastructure:\n\n1. **Command registry** — Extend `src/cli/introspection.ts` to produce a map of command paths to their handler functions and metadata, including a `mutating: boolean` annotation. This enables dynamic dispatch without Commander.js parsing overhead and drives the allow/deny classification.\n\n2. **Batch executor** (`src/cli/batch-exec.ts`) — New module:\n   - `parseBatchInput(source)` — Reads from stdin/file/inline, parses JSON array\n   - `validateBatch(commands, registry, context)` — Pre-validates all commands: known command, required args, ref resolution (including forward refs from earlier commands in batch)\n   - `executeBatch(commands, registry, context, options)` — Executes validated commands sequentially, collects results, handles stop-on-error vs continue\n\n3. **Shadow commit batching** — Use a `context.batchMode` flag. When set, `commitIfShadow()` skips the commit. The batch executor issues a single commit after all operations complete (or after partial completion with `--continue`). The flag is set before execution and cleared after.\n\n4. **Forward reference resolution** — During pre-validation, track slugs that will be created by earlier commands. Build a \"planned refs\" set that the validator checks against when a ref doesn't exist yet. Only tracks creates, not deletes (documented limitation).\n\n5. **Confirmation suppression** — When `context.batchMode` is set, commands that check for `@trait-confirmation-prompt` behavior skip the prompt and proceed as if `--force` were passed.\n\n6. **Handler extraction** — Each command's `.action()` handler needs to be callable programmatically (not just via Commander.js parsing). Extract the core logic into importable functions that batch can call directly. Many commands already follow this pattern (e.g., `resolveTaskRefForBatch()`).\n\n7. **Test approach** — Unit tests for parse/validate/execute phases. Integration test with a temp kspec project running a real batch payload end-to-end. Test the full matrix: stdin/file/inline × stop-on-error/continue × success/failure/partial."
