  {
    "_ulid": "01KGTHJ9JB482P2TH67QF3DQRQ",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Document kspec batch command across docs and skills",
    "type": "task",
    "spec_ref": "@batch-exec",
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #326. Documented kspec batch command across 7 files (SKILL.md, CLAUDE.md, README.md, spec-plan, triage, inbox, observations). Codex review caught arg name errors (content→text/message) and variadic format (string→array) — fixed before merge.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 2,
    "tags": [],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-06T22:36:06.603Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-06T22:37:01.690Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-06T23:10:07.326Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGTHJNS7CRYMWZEJCG1RFYGB",
        "created_at": "2026-02-06T22:36:19.111Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Batch command (PR #324) is fully implemented with spec coverage in cli.yaml (@batch-exec) but has zero documentation in user-facing or agent-facing docs.\n\nDocumentation targets (by priority):\n\nHIGH:\n- .claude/skills/kspec/SKILL.md — Add dedicated 'Batch Operations' section with full command reference, input methods, execution modes, JSON format, use cases\n- CLAUDE.md — Add batch to Quick Start examples section\n- README.md — Add batch to CLI commands section\n\nMEDIUM (topically relevant):\n- .claude/skills/spec-plan/SKILL.md — Note batch for programmatic spec/task creation from plans\n- .claude/skills/triage/SKILL.md + docs/inbox.md — Note batch for bulk triage (promote, resolve, delete)\n- AGENTS.md — Add to command reference areas\n\nLOW:\n- .claude/skills/task-work/SKILL.md — Mention batch in loop mode context\n- .claude/skills/triage/docs/observations.md — Bulk observation resolution\n\nKey content to document:\n- Input: stdin pipe, --file, --commands inline\n- Modes: atomic (default, single commit, rollback) vs immediate (--no-atomic, per-command commits)\n- Flags: --dry-run, --continue (implies --no-atomic)\n- JSON format: {command: '...', args: {...}, id?: '...'} \n- Use cases: bulk triage, plan imports, multi-spec creation, observation batch resolve",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGTHPDAPTFPJK6VR58MPYP3S",
        "created_at": "2026-02-06T22:38:21.526Z",
        "author": "@claude",
