  {
    "_ulid": "01KGVARWDN5AHFD3YXG2W20EZG",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Fix ralph log: String() on array of objects produces [object Object]",
    "type": "task",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #329. Added stringify() helper to handle array-of-content-blocks and plain objects in ralph event output extraction.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 2,
    "tags": [],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-07T05:56:36.917Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-07T06:32:04.575Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-07T06:41:35.003Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGVASA25FCF8BH80S33YDTZ8",
        "created_at": "2026-02-07T05:56:50.885Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "## Bug Report\n\nWhen a subagent completes in the ralph loop, tool results are sometimes rendered as `[object Object],[object Object]` instead of actual content.\n\n### Root Cause\n\n`src/ralph/events.ts` — `extractToolOutput()` and `extractOriginalOutput()` use `String()` to convert values:\n\n- Line 212: `String(update.rawOutput)`\n- Line 229: `String(toolResponse)` (fallback when no stdout)\n- Line 235: `String(update.output)`\n- Lines 248, 266: same pattern in `extractOriginalOutput()`\n\nWhen ACP delivers tool results as an array of content blocks (e.g. `[{type: 'text', text: '...'}, ...]`), `String()` on an array of objects produces `[object Object],[object Object]`.\n\nThe output then flows through `cli-renderer.ts:231-238` which prints it verbatim.\n\n### Fix\n\nAdd a helper function that checks if the value is a string, array, or object, and handles each:\n- String → use as-is\n- Array of content blocks → extract `.text` fields and join\n- Object → `JSON.stringify()`\n\nApply to all 5 `String()` call sites in `extractToolOutput()` and `extractOriginalOutput()`.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGVCWCCJQ8DVEH8K1WJ03V80",
        "created_at": "2026-02-07T06:33:28.723Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Added stringify() helper in events.ts that handles string/array/object values. Replaced all 5 String() call sites in extractToolOutput() and extractOriginalOutput(). Arrays of content blocks (e.g. [{type:'text',text:'...'}]) now extract .text fields and join with newlines. Plain objects get JSON.stringify(). Added 3 test cases covering array-of-blocks, single-block, and plain-object scenarios.",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
  },
  {
    "_ulid": "01KGVAZ6ZXXCBK1DYJ4GF4FRAM",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Fix: 'No onPostToolUseHook found' leaks past noise suppression",
    "type": "task",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #345. Fixed noise suppression for hook warnings by changing from skip-entire-chunk to strip-patterns strategy. The stripNoise function now removes noise patterns from content while preserving surrounding text, handling both standalone noise and embedded noise concatenated with agent messages. Added comprehensive tests covering whitespace preservation, greedy matching prevention, and cross-chunk accumulation.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 3,
    "tags": [],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-07T06:00:04.348Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-07T13:40:47.394Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-07T14:14:15.729Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGVAZPBDYHGH6XKKK5BWB0WR",
        "created_at": "2026-02-07T06:00:20.077Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "## Bug Report\n\n`No onPostToolUseHook found for tool use ID: toolu_...` appears in ralph output despite existing suppression pattern.\n\n### What exists\n\n`src/ralph/events.ts:304-307` has SUPPRESSED_PATTERNS including `/No onPostToolUseHook found/i`.\n`shouldSuppress()` is called at lines 355 and 405 — but ONLY for `agent_message_chunk` and `agent_thought_chunk` update types.\n\n### Likely cause\n\nThe hook message is arriving through a code path that bypasses the suppression check. Possible scenarios:\n1. It arrives as a different ACP update type (not message/thought chunk)\n2. It arrives concatenated with normal agent text in the same chunk — suppressing the whole chunk would lose good content, so the check needs to strip the noise substring rather than suppress the entire chunk\n3. It comes through stderr or a side channel that doesn't go through the translator\n\n### Observed output\n```\nExcellent creative brief. Now launching Phase 2...No onPostToolUseHook found for tool use ID: toolu_01LCkxN6GwoWUfvy7wqwp3sW\n```\n\nNote the concatenation with no newline — suggests it's in the same streaming content.\n\n### Suggested fix\n\nChange suppression from 'skip entire chunk' to 'strip matching patterns from chunk content'. This handles both standalone noise chunks and noise embedded in real content.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGW5M9FFRTW507CG7MKWFSYW",
        "created_at": "2026-02-07T13:45:57.999Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Fixed by changing suppression strategy from skip-entire-chunk to strip-patterns. The stripNoise function now removes noise patterns from content while preserving surrounding text. This handles the observed bug where hook warnings were concatenated directly with agent messages (no newline). Added tests for: standalone noise suppression, embedded noise stripping, multiple patterns in same chunk, and accumulation across chunks.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGW6PQP7Z3WN0V476PWQQFVZ",
        "created_at": "2026-02-07T14:04:46.664Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Known limitation: Split-chunk noise during streaming cannot be fully suppressed because text is emitted before the complete pattern is known. The fix ensures final accumulated content is clean at finalization. Streaming output is ephemeral and scrolls away, so this is acceptable.",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "automation": "eligible",
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
  },
  {
    "_ulid": "01KGVB8X9Y04BFEYGJAJTTNEBS",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Increase ralph loop prompt timeout from 5min to 30min",
    "type": "task",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #328. Added RALPH_PROMPT_TIMEOUT (30min) override for both ralph agent and subagent spawn sites.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 2,
    "tags": [],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-07T06:05:22.110Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-07T06:06:33.409Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-07T06:23:24.142Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGVB9DDRX1V0E61VRSHC1853",
        "created_at": "2026-02-07T06:05:38.616Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "## Context\n\nThe ACP framing layer at `src/acp/framing.ts:64-67` sets a 5-minute (300,000ms) timeout for `session/prompt` and `session/resume` methods. The timer resets on any agent activity (tool calls, notifications) via `resetPendingTimers()` at line 245.\n\nHowever, the 5-minute default is too aggressive for ralph loop usage. The agent can go silent for extended periods due to:\n- Anthropic API slowness/throttling\n- Extended thinking on complex tasks\n- Large context processing before first output\n\n### Proposed fix\n\nThe ralph loop should override the default timeout when spawning agents. Options:\n1. Pass a higher `methodTimeouts` override in `JsonRpcFramingOptions` when creating the framing layer for ralph agents (preferred — keeps default reasonable for non-ralph usage)\n2. Increase the default globally (less ideal — 30min is too long for general use)\n\nThe framing constructor already supports overrides via `options.methodTimeouts` (line 94-97), so ralph just needs to pass `{ 'session/prompt': 30 * 60 * 1000 }` through the spawner.\n\n### Files\n- `src/acp/framing.ts` — timeout defaults and override mechanism\n- `src/ralph/index.ts` or `src/cli/commands/ralph.ts` — where agents are spawned\n- `src/agents/spawner.ts` — may need to thread timeout options through",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGVBKERPD0GFY7W34V0GAMDD",
        "created_at": "2026-02-07T06:11:07.671Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "## Implementation\n\nAdded `RALPH_PROMPT_TIMEOUT` constant (30 minutes) in `src/ralph/subagent.ts` and applied it to both ACP agent spawn sites:\n\n1. **Main ralph agent** (`src/cli/commands/ralph.ts:1235`) — `clientOptions.methodTimeouts` override for `session/prompt` and `session/resume`\n2. **Review subagent** (`src/ralph/subagent.ts:173`) — same override\n\nThe framing layer's constructor already merges user-provided `methodTimeouts` over defaults (line 94-97), so this cleanly overrides the 5-minute default without touching the default for non-ralph usage.\n\nExported through `src/ralph/index.ts`.\n\nAll 104 ralph tests + 43 ACP tests pass.",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
  },
