    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGYC0EHBTS85BWHV7SRM5PCF",
        "created_at": "2026-02-08T10:15:56.715Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "## Context\n\nPR kynetic-ai/kynetic-bot#90 restructured kynetic-bot's AGENTS.md from 287 → 496 lines, \nmodeled on kynetic-spec's tightened AGENTS.md (PR #350). Codex reviewed the PR and found \n5 issues — all fixed. Several patterns discovered during that work should be back-ported \nto kynetic-spec's AGENTS.md.\n\n## Findings That Translate\n\n### 1. MUST-FIX: Verify doc claims against source code\nCodex caught that AGENTS.md claimed supervisor \"Notifies ESCALATION_CHANNEL\" but code only \nemits/logs. **Audit kynetic-spec AGENTS.md for similar claim-vs-reality gaps**, especially \nin Running Services, Shadow Branch Architecture, and Test Fixture Patterns sections.\n\n### 2. SHOULD-FIX: Distinguish auto-commit mechanisms\nkynetic-spec rule 1 says \"CLI auto-commits to shadow branch\" which is accurate since it only \nhas .kspec/. But if/when kynetic-spec adds runtime data (e.g., web-ui sessions), the same \nambiguity would appear. Low priority — just awareness.\n\n### 3. SHOULD-FIX: PR agent limitations note\nkynetic-bot AGENTS.md added: \"PR agent limitations: Review subagent can't run kspec/npm — \nmust delegate those to main agent.\" This is equally true for kynetic-spec but not documented. \nAdd to PR Workflow section.\n\n### 4. SHOULD-FIX: Dual defaults documentation pattern\nkynetic-bot had SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT defaulting to 10s in bot config but 30s in supervisor CLI. \nCheck kynetic-spec for similar split-default env vars (daemon port, health check intervals) \nand document explicitly if found.\n\n### 5. SUGGESTION: Consolidate duplicate guidance\nkynetic-bot had \"Creating Work\" duplicated in two sections. Check kynetic-spec for similar \nredundancy — the \"Creating Work\" subsection under Spec-First Development exists, verify \nnothing overlaps elsewhere.\n\n### 6. SUGGESTION: Add bot-style \"Running\" gotchas section\nkynetic-spec's Running Services section could benefit from explicit gotchas like:\n- E2E port hardcoded (already in CI Limitations table but not in Running)\n- daemon health endpoint path\n- web-ui BASE_PATH requirement for local static builds\n\n## What Was Done in kynetic-bot#90\n\n- Rewrote AGENTS.md: 20 sections, ~496 lines\n- Slimmed CLAUDE.md to single `@AGENTS.md` directive\n- New sections: project identity, dual shadow branches, bot architecture (ACP/supervisor/memory), ralph loop mode, PR workflow, running the bot, expanded troubleshooting\n- Codex review found 5 issues, all fixed in follow-up commit\n- All review threads resolved, CI green, merged",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGZXJ0YCQSZQP2KA3XPX97ND",
        "created_at": "2026-02-09T00:41:52.844Z",
