    "created_at": "2026-02-09T00:41:14.336Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KGZXHPGRK690BSKDEVFW6529",
        "created_at": "2026-02-09T00:41:42.168Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "## Goal\n\nRestructure imgen's AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md to match the kynetic-spec/kynetic-bot standard:\nlean doc with architecture/gotchas/decision frameworks, skills carry workflow detail, \nCLAUDE.md is just `@AGENTS.md`.\n\n## Reference: kynetic-bot#90\n\nPR kynetic-ai/kynetic-bot#90 completed this same work for kynetic-bot. Key patterns:\n\n### Section structure (20 sections, adapt as needed for imgen)\n1. What This Project Is — package overview with responsibilities\n2. Finding Information — skill routing table\n3. Quick Start — prerequisites, install, env vars\n4. Essential Rules — 6 numbered rules (CLI not YAML, spec before code, etc.)\n5. Project Structure — file tree\n6. Shadow Branch Architecture — .kspec/ worktree explanation\n7. Project-Specific Architecture — the core of what makes imgen unique\n8. Key Concepts — IDs, spec vs tasks, task states, notes\n9. Task Workflow — session start, working, creating work\n10. Session Context & Observations — focus/observe/thread + types table\n11. Spec-First Development — decision table, plan mode workflow, creating work\n12. Staying Aligned — scope expansion guardrails\n13. PR Workflow — 3-step lifecycle, quality gates, PR agent limitations note\n14. Commit Convention — trailers\n15. Code Annotations — AC test links\n16. Ralph Loop Mode — loop, task inheritance, blocking rules\n17. Running/Development — how to run the project, env vars, gotchas\n18. Workflows — table of all defined workflows\n19. Troubleshooting — expanded table\n20. Environment — KSPEC_AUTHOR\n\n### Codex review findings that apply universally\n- **Verify doc claims against source code** — don't document behavior that isn't implemented\n- **Distinguish auto-commit mechanisms** if project has multiple shadow branches\n- **Document dual defaults** when same env var has different defaults in different contexts\n- **PR agent limitations** — \"Review subagent can't run kspec/npm\" applies to all projects\n- **Consolidate duplicate guidance** — check for redundant \"Creating Work\" or similar sections\n- **Gotchas section in Running** — document things that silently fail or confuse\n\n### CLAUDE.md\nReplace with single line: `@AGENTS.md`\nMigrate any unique content into the appropriate AGENTS.md section first.\n\n## Process\n1. Read imgen's current AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md\n2. Read imgen source code for project-specific architecture, gotchas, env vars\n3. Write new AGENTS.md following the section template above\n4. Replace CLAUDE.md with `@AGENTS.md`\n5. Run /codex review on the PR for factual accuracy cross-check\n6. Address findings, resolve threads, merge\n\n## Verification checklist\n- wc -l AGENTS.md within ±20 of target (estimate after reading current state)\n- wc -l CLAUDE.md = 1 line\n- Kspec self-sufficiency: agent can start session, translate plans, follow ralph rules\n- Project-specific: covers unique architecture, env vars, development gotchas\n- No skill duplication: AGENTS has frameworks, skills have procedures\n- Codex review passes with no MUST-FIX items",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHD0KJZ8QD0G8T9CG6D6ESWA",
        "created_at": "2026-02-14T02:45:17.417Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Automation status set to manual_only: Documentation restructuring for external project - requires human judgment",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "automation": "manual_only",
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
  },
