  {
    "_ulid": "01KHA83PTDMSSA5N4EX7KZ6QAP",
    "slugs": [
      "implement-output-format-option"
    ],
    "title": "Implement Output Format Option",
    "type": "task",
    "spec_ref": "@output-format-option",
    "plan_ref": "@plan-cli-agent-ux-improvements",
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #364. Implemented output format shorthands (--json, --yaml, --raw) as global CLI options. Added YAML output support using the yaml library. Conflict detection for multiple format shorthands. 13 tests covering all ACs except ac-unsupported-format (not applicable since --format is not global due to Commander.js limitations with child command option shadowing).",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 3,
    "tags": [],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-13T00:58:42.381Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-14T09:40:20.956Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-14T10:02:05.615Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHA83PTEA3F4F1TWC7F342Z8",
        "created_at": "2026-02-13T00:58:42.382Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implementation notes:\n\nRegister --format <format> as a global option alongside --json in index.ts.\nRegister --raw and --yaml as boolean shorthands that set format. In the\npreAction hook, resolve shorthands to --format value, detect conflicts\n(multiple shorthands or shorthand + --format), then call setJsonMode() or\na new setYamlMode(). Add yamlOutput() in output.ts using the yaml library\nstringify(). Update output() to check yaml mode. Update @trait-json-output\nac-6 to reference the --format system instead of the old json takes\nprecedence behavior.\n"
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHDS2WSABSAXDMX7G3ZQ16Y9",
        "created_at": "2026-02-14T09:53:04.810Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implemented output format shorthands (--json, --yaml, --raw) as global options.\n\nNote: The --format <format> option cannot be global due to Commander.js limitations - when a parent command defines an option, it shadows child command options with the same name. The export command has its own --format option for different purposes (json, html), so global --format would conflict.\n\nImplementation:\n- Added setYamlMode(), isYamlMode(), isStructuredMode() to output.ts\n- Added YAML output support using the yaml library's stringify()\n- Updated output(), success(), error(), warn(), info() to support YAML format\n- Added --json, --yaml, --raw as global shorthands in index.ts preAction hook\n- Conflict detection for multiple format shorthands\n- 13 tests covering: JSON/YAML output, shorthands equivalence, conflict errors, global scope\n\nACs covered:\n- ac-format-json: --json produces valid JSON ✓\n- ac-format-yaml: --yaml produces valid YAML ✓\n- ac-json-shorthand: --json works globally ✓\n- ac-raw-shorthand: --raw = --json ✓\n- ac-yaml-shorthand: --yaml works globally ✓\n- ac-conflict-error: Multiple format shorthands error ✓\n- ac-yaml-no-ansi: YAML output has no ANSI codes ✓\n- ac-yaml-references: @ prefix preserved in YAML ✓\n- ac-global-scope: Works on item list, tasks ready, session start ✓\n- ac-unsupported-format: Not applicable (--format not global)",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "automation": "eligible",
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
  },
  {
