    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #365. Implemented --under flag for module-scoped item listing. Added findDescendantItems() function to find items by _path prefix within same source file. All 8 acceptance criteria have test coverage in tests/item-list-under.test.ts. Flag works with --tree, --count, --json, and combines with other filters using AND logic.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 3,
    "tags": [],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-13T00:58:42.761Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-14T10:02:32.785Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-14T10:19:09.277Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHA83Q69VGE1B8PN321177M2",
        "created_at": "2026-02-13T00:58:42.761Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implementation notes:\n\nItems do NOT have a parent field in the schema. Parent-child hierarchy is\ndetermined by YAML nesting, encoded in the _path metadata field (e.g.\nfeatures[0].requirements[1]). The existing formatItemTree() in item.ts\n(lines 121-177) builds parent-child maps by parsing _path. The existing\nfindChildItems() in parser/items.ts (lines 422-455) finds direct children\nonly -- extend it or build a new findDescendantItems() that collects all\nitems sharing the same _sourceFile whose _path starts with the target\n_path prefix. Resolve --under ref via ReferenceIndex, find the target\n_sourceFile and _path, then filter the item list. Apply other filters\nafter scoping.\n"
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHDT1HNMPEYHBCP0P429467T",
        "created_at": "2026-02-14T10:09:49.237Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implemented --under flag for module-scoped item listing:\n\n- Added findDescendantItems() function in parser/items.ts that finds all items sharing the same _sourceFile with a _path prefix matching the parent\n- Updated item list command to accept --under <ref> option\n- Reference resolution with error handling for invalid/task references\n- Proper pagination handling (queries all items, then filters by scope, then applies limit)\n- Works with --tree flag for hierarchical display\n- Works with --count flag to show scoped subtree count\n- Combines with other filters using AND logic\n- JSON output includes all items in subtree\n\n12 tests covering all 8 ACs:\n- ac-under-filter: Only descendants shown\n- ac-under-root-included: Root item included\n- ac-nested-descendants: Multi-level nesting works\n- ac-under-with-tree: Tree display scoped correctly\n- ac-under-with-other-filters: AND logic with type/status filters\n- ac-under-json: Full item data in JSON\n- ac-under-invalid-ref: Error with suggestion message\n- ac-count-with-under: Count reflects scoped subtree",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "automation": "eligible",
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
  },
