        "content": "Implemented kspec refs command for unified cross-reference lookup:\n\n- New command file src/cli/commands/refs.ts\n- Scans tasks and spec items for all reference fields: spec_ref, depends_on, meta_ref, plan_ref, blocked_by, implements, relates_to, supersedes, traits, tests\n- Groups output by relationship type (e.g., 'Tasks (spec_ref)', 'Specs (depends_on)')\n- Supports --json flag with structured output containing keys per reference type\n- Uses ReferenceIndex that includes meta items (workflows, agents, etc.) for full reference resolution\n- Supports ULID, slug, and short ULID reference formats\n- Shows 'No references found' message for isolated items (exit code 0)\n\n14 tests covering all 12 ACs:\n- ac-task-spec-ref: Tasks with spec_ref pointing to target\n- ac-task-depends-on: Tasks with depends_on including target\n- ac-spec-depends-on: Specs with depends_on including target\n- ac-spec-implements: Specs with implements including target\n- ac-spec-relates-to: Specs with relates_to including target\n- ac-trait-references: Specs with traits including target\n- ac-meta-ref: Tasks with meta_ref pointing to target\n- ac-supersedes: Specs with supersedes pointing to target\n- ac-grouped-output: Section headers like 'Specs (depends on)'\n- ac-json-structured: JSON keys per reference type with proper structure\n- ac-no-refs: No references found message\n- ac-ref-resolution: ULID, slug, and short ULID formats",
