    "title": "Distinguish graceful exit from abort in task-work-loop workflow",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "Distinguish graceful exit from abort in task-work-loop: when the workflow exits because no eligible tasks exist, record as status:completed with result:no_work_available instead of status:aborted. Makes abort rate meaningful (actual failures) vs normal loop termination. Data: 11 of 16 'aborts' were normal no-work exits, inflating abort rate to 69%.",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #355. Added 'kspec workflow complete' command with --result option supporting success, no_work_available, and early_exit results. This allows distinguishing graceful loop termination (no_work_available) from actual failures (abort), making abort rate metrics meaningful. Added WorkflowRunResultSchema to schema and 14 tests covering all scenarios.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 3,
    "tags": [],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-13T05:06:15.997Z",
