    "title": "Fix: auto-prefix @ on depends_on reference values",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "Bug: task set --depends-on and task add --depends-on store raw ID without @ prefix, breaking dependency resolution. When running 'kspec task set @foo --depends-on 01KH7XA9' (no @), the YAML stores 'depends_on: [01KH7XA9]' instead of '- @01KH7XA9'. This makes the task invisible to task get/tasks list because the dependency resolver can't find the reference. All working depends_on entries in the wild use @-prefixed slugs or ULIDs. Fix: either auto-prefix @ on depends-on values, or validate/reject bare IDs with a helpful error. Discovered in imgen project session 13.",
    "spec_ref": "@rel-depends-on",
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #353. Auto-prefixes @ on bare depends_on refs in task add, task set, and derive commands. 3 new tests confirm bare slugs and ULIDs are stored with @ prefix.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 3,
    "tags": [
      "bug",
      "cli"
    ],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-13T05:12:10.715Z",
