    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Fix: ralph noise stripping leaks on split-chunk boundaries",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "PR #345 ralph noise stripping: split-chunk noise leaks to streaming output before finalization. When noise phrase is split across chunk boundaries (e.g. 'No onPostToolUse' + 'Hook found for tool use ID: toolu_...'), both chunks emit as streaming events. Need boundary-aware buffering in createTranslator. Also: stripped-to-whitespace should return null. See /tmp/codex-pr-345-review.md for full analysis.",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #356. Implemented boundary-aware buffering in createTranslator to handle noise patterns split across streaming chunk boundaries. Added noiseBuffer to TranslatorState, processChunkWithBuffer() for partial pattern detection before stripping, and getPartialNoiseLength() for detecting incomplete patterns. 7 new tests cover split scenarios at various pattern boundaries and false-positive detection.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 3,
    "tags": [
      "ralph",
      "noise",
      "streaming"
    ],
    "vcs_refs": [],
