    "started_at": "2026-02-14T02:59:51.802Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-14T03:17:31.790Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHASR8CAMRSTZSBJ5537JF3W",
        "created_at": "2026-02-13T06:07:01.514Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Bug: noise phrases split across chunk boundaries (e.g. 'No onPostToolUse' + 'Hook found for tool use ID: toolu_...') both emit as streaming events. Need boundary-aware buffering in createTranslator. Also: stripped-to-whitespace should return null. Analysis from PR #345 Codex review.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHD1W8Y1WM63K2FH6YTRDTXJ",
        "created_at": "2026-02-14T03:07:30.625Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implemented boundary-aware buffering in createTranslator to handle noise patterns split across chunk boundaries. Key changes: (1) Added noiseBuffer to TranslatorState, (2) Created processChunkWithBuffer() that checks for partial noise patterns BEFORE stripping complete patterns, (3) Added getPartialNoiseLength() to detect when content ends with a potential partial noise pattern. 7 new tests covering split-chunk scenarios including partial at 'No onPostToolUse', partial tool IDs, multi-split patterns, and false-positive detection.",
        "supersedes": null
      }
