        "content": "Implemented skill drift detection with all 5 acceptance criteria:\n\n- ac-1: Skills show as in-sync when rendered file matches stored hash\n- ac-2: Skills show as drifted when rendered file has been manually edited (hash mismatch)\n- ac-3: Drifted skills are skipped with warning when rendering without --force\n- ac-4: --force option overwrites drifted files and updates the hash\n- ac-5: Hash of rendered output is stored in .kspec/skills/<id>/.render-hash\n\nImplementation uses SHA256 hash for change detection. Added 16 new tests covering all ACs plus edge cases (legacy renders without hash, mixed drift states, etc).",
