    "title": "Implement: Setup Pipeline Unification",
    "type": "task",
    "spec_ref": "@setup-pipeline-unification",
    "derivation": "auto",
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #405. Follow-up fixes for Codex review in PR #406. All 5 ACs implemented: setup uses generateAgentsContent from agents.ts, platform renderer registry, single runSetupPipeline code path, debug logging on all catch blocks, init --setup and setup use same pipeline.",
    "depends_on": [
      "@task-dead-code-and-deduplication-sweep"
    ],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 2,
    "tags": [],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-18T06:43:37.020Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-18T09:17:38.241Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-18T14:44:43.592Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHQQTVDVQ3V8P5414ZHXKZ97",
        "created_at": "2026-02-18T06:43:37.019Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implementation notes (auto-generated from spec):\n\nUnify the setup command to use the same code paths as the rest of the CLI instead of reimplementing agent instruction generation and skill rendering. Highest impact for portable install - new projects currently get output from divergent code paths.\n\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n- ac-1: Given setup.ts needs to generate agent instructions, when the setup pipeline runs, then it calls the exported generateAgentsContent() from agents.ts (not a local reimplementation)\n- ac-2: Given setup.ts needs to render skills, when the setup pipeline renders skills for any platform, then it uses the platform renderer registry (getRenderer/getAllRenderers) not the legacy renderClaudeCodeSkill\n- ac-3: Given the setup command is invoked, when the command handler executes, then it delegates to runSetupPipeline() - there is one code path, not two parallel implementations\n- ac-4: Given any setup step throws an error, when a catch block handles it, then the error is logged at debug level (not silently swallowed with bare catch {})\n- ac-5: Given a new project runs kspec init --setup, when setup completes, then the output is identical to running kspec setup separately (same code path)",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHR13053N4A48CTKXMBRJ811",
        "created_at": "2026-02-18T09:25:21.187Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "All 5 ACs implemented:\n\n- AC-1: generateAgentInstructions() in setup.ts now calls generateAgentsContent(), loadTemplateSections(), getPackageRoot(), and computeMetaHash() from agents.ts instead of reimplementing them locally. These functions were exported from agents.ts.\n- AC-2: renderSkillsForSetup() now uses getRenderer() from the platform renderer registry instead of directly importing renderClaudeCodeSkill. Renders skills for all platforms with registered renderers.\n- AC-3: The command handler in registerSetupCommand() now delegates to runSetupPipeline() instead of duplicating the pipeline steps inline. Author config was added to the pipeline options.\n- AC-4: All 13+ bare catch {} blocks in setup.ts replaced with catch (err) { debugLog(..., err) } that logs at debug level (KSPEC_DEBUG=1). Static analysis test verifies no bare catch blocks remain.\n- AC-5: kspec init --setup and kspec setup both call runSetupPipeline() with the same options, producing identical artifacts.",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
  },
