  {
    "_ulid": "01KHVJ59J39YXKFWAFTJY10YER",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Triage skills for core portability",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "Review all 24+ skills in .claude/skills/ and categorize each into: (1) Core — ships in templates/skills/ for any kspec project (e.g. task-work, pr, spec, meta, triage, reflect, local-review, spec-plan, kspec), (2) Project-specific but portable — useful pattern but contains kspec-project-specific content that would need generalization (e.g. e2e, svelte-5, eval-agents), (3) Not portable — only makes sense for this project (e.g. codex with shadow-branch workarounds). For each skill, document: current category, what would need to change to make it core, and any dependencies on other skills. Output should be a clear manifest of what ships as core vs stays project-local.",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Triage complete. Created 11 follow-up tasks for core skill namespace work.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 2,
    "tags": [],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-19T18:21:25.437Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-21T05:46:58.841Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-21T07:31:10.039Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHW11A371KAK7CHYSYQGPYW1",
        "created_at": "2026-02-19T22:41:23.559Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Automation status set to manual_only: Spike — output is categorization manifest, requires human judgment on core vs project-local",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHZBXH96AQ3WHJGRS9RYZ554",
        "created_at": "2026-02-21T05:49:17.479Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Triage completed. Three categories identified:\n\n**Core (ship with kspec) — 13 skills:**\nkspec, meta, reflect, triage, spec, spec-plan, task-work, pr, pr-review, local-review, create-workflow, audit, release\n\n**Project-specific (kynetic-spec only) — 3 skills:**\ne2e (Playwright/SvelteKit web UI), svelte-5 (Svelte 5 patterns), eval-agents (AGENTS.md eval with project-specific scenarios)\n\n**Not kspec-managed — external:**\ncodex (Codex CLI integration, SKILL.md but not in kspec skill registry), .claude/hooks/ (worktree guard, ralph task limit), .claude/settings*.json\n\n**Key findings:**\n- All 17 skills live in .claude/skills/ as Claude Code native SKILL.md files, NOT kspec-managed skills (kspec skill list shows only 1 core skill: kspec-help)\n- The 13 core skills ARE the kspec agent workflow — without them agents have no task/PR/review guidance\n- codex is an edge case: external tool integration pattern, could be an optional integration template\n- release assumes npm publish but the pattern is broadly applicable\n- Hooks (worktree guard, ralph task limit) are also candidates for shipping with kspec setup\n- Next steps: decide how to ship core skills (kspec setup installs them? kspec skill install --core?), then implement",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHZG0QP9MAF8SV79ZHPVCZ5Z",
        "created_at": "2026-02-21T07:00:56.650Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Session 2 update - refined triage with user input. Final categorization:\n\n**Core kspec skills (10, namespaced under .claude/skills/kspec/):**\n- /kspec:help — lean CLI map, merge current kspec+kspec-help, instruct agents to use kspec help <cmd>\n- /kspec:observations — renamed from meta, covers friction/success/idea capture and promotion (focus/threads may be purged)\n- /kspec:reflect — session reflection\n- /kspec:triage-inbox — inbox item triage (split from monolithic triage)\n- /kspec:triage-automation — task automation eligibility (split from monolithic triage)\n- /kspec:writing-specs — renamed from spec, AC/trait/module authoring\n- /kspec:plan — renamed from spec-plan, plan-to-spec translation\n- /kspec:task-work — task lifecycle and work loop\n- /kspec:create-workflow — meta-workflow for formalizing patterns\n- /kspec:review — NEW, extracted kspec-specific review: spec/AC alignment, trait AC coverage, kspec validate, coding best practices for kspec workflow\n\n**Project-specific (stay in .claude/skills/ root, NOT core):**\naudit, pr, pr-review, local-review, release, e2e, svelte-5, eval-agents, codex\n\n**Key decisions:**\n- pr, pr-review, local-review must be PURGED from templates/agents-sections and any shared docs — they are project-specific\n- Namespace support needs spec+code work: colon separator, nested dirs, user-installable namespaces\n- kspec setup should install core skills into .claude/skills/kspec/\n- Next: /spec-plan to spec out namespace support and create the core skills",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHZGQYSH68NZBAQH68MXW1HA",
        "created_at": "2026-02-21T07:13:37.585Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Clarification: namespace support is NOT a code change — Claude Code natively supports nested skill dirs (.claude/skills/kspec/help/SKILL.md → /kspec:help). No schema or parser work needed. Work is: create core SKILL.md files, update kspec setup to install them, purge project-specific refs from shared docs. Awaiting user decision on whether to spec-plan or start writing directly.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHZGVGE76EYG3P1KQ6NG4VYR",
        "created_at": "2026-02-21T07:15:33.959Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Session 2 continued — investigated existing core skill infrastructure:\n\n**What exists (fully built):**\n- templates/skills/manifest.yaml defines core skills (currently only kspec-help)\n- kspec setup calls installCoreSkillsForSetup() → reads manifest, copies SKILL.md to .kspec/skills/<id>/\n- renderSkillsForSetup() renders to .claude/skills/<id>/SKILL.md\n- kspec skill install-core and kspec skill update commands exist\n- Skill id validated by KEBAB_CASE_REGEX: /^[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$/ — NO slashes or colons\n\n**What needs to change for namespacing:**\n- Claude Code natively handles nested dirs: .claude/skills/kspec/help/SKILL.md → /kspec:help\n- Two approaches: (A) keep flat id in schema, add namespace field that controls render path, or (B) allow slash in id regex so kspec/help naturally creates nested dirs\n- getRenderedSkillPath() currently does: .claude/skills/<id>/ — needs to handle namespace\n- Template structure: templates/skills/kspec-help/ → templates/skills/kspec/help/\n- All 10 core skills need SKILL.md content written\n\n**Next step: /spec-plan to design the namespace schema + render changes + write all 10 skills**",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "automation": "manual_only",
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
