  {
    "_ulid": "01KHVK28M6TAWG0YV55XYMM33D",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Generalize agent template sections for consumer projects",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "The 6 template files in templates/agents-sections/ are used by 'kspec agents generate' to produce kspec-agents.md for any project. Currently they contain kspec-repo-specific references that break on consumer projects.\n\n## Evidence from consumer projects (kynetic-bot, imgen, comfy-ecaj-nodes)\n\nAll three consumers copy-paste these sections verbatim into their AGENTS.md because the generated output isn't right. They all independently converged on the same Quick Start pattern:\n```bash\nkspec init          # first time\nkspec setup         # configure agent environment  \nkspec session start # get context\n```\n\nNone use bootstrap.cjs or npm run dev. All three have the same hooks pattern (prompt-check, checkpoint, worktree-guard). All suffer from stale copies when upstream templates change.\n\n## Specific fixes needed per file\n\n**01-quick-start.md** (CRITICAL):\n- Replace 'node scripts/bootstrap.cjs' with generic 'kspec init && kspec setup' \n- Remove 'npm run dev --' reference (kspec-repo-only)\n- Add 'kspec session start' as the returning-session command\n- Consider mentioning 'kspec shadow status' for health verification\n\n**02-shadow-branch.md**: Already generic. No changes needed.\n\n**03-task-lifecycle.md**: Already generic. No changes needed.\n\n**04-pr-workflow.md**: Already generic. No changes needed.\n\n**05-commit-convention.md**:\n- Code annotation example is TypeScript-only (`// AC: @spec-item ac-N`)\n- Should be language-agnostic or show both styles (// for TS/JS, # for Python/Ruby/Shell)\n- comfy-ecaj-nodes uses '# AC:' pattern already\n\n**06-ralph-loop.md**: Already generic. No changes needed.\n\n## Additional considerations\n\n- Consumer AGENTS.md files range from 358 (kspec) to 710 lines (imgen) — the generated output should be lean since projects add their own domain content on top\n- The 'Finding Information' skill table in kspec's AGENTS.md is duplicated by all consumers with project-specific skills added — consider generating this table dynamically from installed skills\n- All consumers have project-specific sections (architecture, tech stack, testing patterns) that live OUTSIDE the generated sections — the template output should compose well with custom content",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #414. Generalized agent template sections for consumer projects: (1) 01-quick-start.md now uses generic kspec init/setup pattern instead of kspec-repo-specific bootstrap.cjs, added shadow status tip; (2) 05-commit-convention.md now shows language-agnostic AC annotation examples (JavaScript and Python). Tests updated to verify generic content and reject repo-specific commands.",
