    "type": "task",
    "description": "setup.ts has accumulated tech debt that will cause drift as the render pipeline evolves. Three clusters of issues from inbox items:\n\n## 1. Code duplication in setup pipeline\n- setup.ts reimplements agent instruction generation instead of calling agents.ts generateAgentsContent()\n- Duplicates core skill installation logic from skill.ts\n- Two code paths that will drift over time\n(Inbox: @01KHJ4RV)\n\n## 2. Legacy render path\n- renderClaudeCodeSkill diverges from claudeCodeRenderer: uses old writeRenderHash (not platform-specific), lacks outputDir support, returns old type\n- setup.ts still calls the legacy function instead of routing through registry\n- Should deprecate standalone function and route through registry\n(Inbox: @01KHJ4RV, @01KHKTNJ)\n\n## 3. Error handling and staleness\n- Multiple bare catch {} blocks in setup.ts lose diagnostic info — should log at debug/verbose level\n- getSetupStatus always reports 'current' if hash file exists, cannot detect staleness — should compare hash against current meta context\n(Inbox: @01KHJ4RV, @01KHKTNJ)\n\n## Related items (can address opportunistically)\n- Naming inconsistency: isKspecManagedSkill vs isKspecManaged for same logic (@01KHKTNJ)\n- Dead code: toKebabCase in skill-render.ts never called (@01KHJ4RV)\n- Renderer duplication: Codex and Claude Code renderers share ~70% logic (@01KHKTNJ)\n- Utility dedup: contentsEqual/directoriesEqual/copyDirectory duplicated between skill.ts and skill-render.ts (@01KHJ4RV)",
