        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implementation notes:\n\nWire ctx.config.validation into ValidateOptions in src/parser/validate.ts.\nThe validate command handler in src/cli/commands/validate.ts merges CLI flags\nover config values before calling validate(). Current ValidateOptions has boolean\ntoggles — map strict_refs to the existing strictness behavior and add\nrequire_acceptance as a new check that promotes completeness warnings to errors.\n"
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHWEGVDQXCS1BF5H9AV9TX62",
        "created_at": "2026-02-20T02:37:04.312Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implementation complete. Changes:\n\n1. **Config schema updated** (src/parser/config.ts):\n   - Changed validation config from strictness/warn_unknown_fields to strict_refs/require_acceptance\n   - strict_refs defaults to true (preserves existing behavior - dangling refs are errors)\n   - require_acceptance defaults to false (preserves existing behavior - missing AC is warning)\n\n2. **Validate function updated** (src/parser/validate.ts):\n   - Added strictRefs and requireAcceptance to ValidateOptions\n   - When strictRefs=false, demotes not_found ref errors to warnings\n   - When requireAcceptance=true, promotes missing_acceptance_criteria warnings to errors\n\n3. **CLI wiring** (src/cli/commands/validate.ts):\n   - Passes ctx.config.validation.strict_refs to validate()\n   - Passes ctx.config.validation.require_acceptance to validate()\n   - CLI --strict flag still overrides config for orphans/staleness\n\n4. **Tests added** (tests/parser/validate-config.test.ts):\n   - 7 tests covering all 4 ACs\n   - Tests for require_acceptance behavior (AC-1)\n   - Tests for strict_refs behavior (AC-2, AC-3)\n   - Tests for CLI override behavior (AC-4)\n   - Tests for combined settings\n\n5. **Existing tests updated** (tests/parser/config.test.ts):\n   - Updated to use new field names\n   - Updated default assertions\n\nAll 2885 tests pass (1 pre-existing failure in daemon-executable.test.ts unrelated to this change).",
        "supersedes": null
