  {
    "_ulid": "01KHW2GZAZJ79CJ37JJ78GVGKH",
    "slugs": [
      "impl-doctor-command"
    ],
    "title": "Implement kspec doctor command",
    "type": "task",
    "spec_ref": "@doctor-command",
    "plan_ref": "@plan-unified-health-check-command-kspec-doctor",
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #423. Implemented kspec doctor command with unified health checks for shadow branch, setup (hooks, skills, agents.md), and daemon status. Library layer in src/parser/doctor.ts with CLI command in src/cli/commands/doctor.ts. All 14 ACs covered with 27 tests. Fixed ac-daemon-unreachable test coverage during PR review.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 3,
    "tags": [
      "cli",
      "dx"
    ],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-19T23:07:25.407Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-20T03:29:58.540Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-20T03:54:31.134Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHW2Q8H6Z8BXN6X1V4F9G6EE",
        "created_at": "2026-02-19T23:10:51.430Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implementation notes from plan @plan-unified-health-check-command-kspec-doctor:\n\n**Severity model:** Each check gets ok | warning | error. Shadow broken = error. Setup missing = error. Daemon not running = warning. Staleness unknown = warning. Exit 0 when no errors (warnings are fine). Exit 1 when any error exists.\n\n**Library layer: src/parser/doctor.ts (new)**\nPlace alongside existing parser modules (src/parser/shadow.ts, src/parser/yaml.ts). Returns DoctorReport with CheckResult per subsystem.\n\nFlow:\n1. getShadowStatus(projectRoot) — if !exists, return early with not-initialized report\n2. If shadow exists, run setup + daemon in parallel via Promise.allSettled\n3. For setup: call getSetupStatus(projectRoot) — fix staleness bug (unknown, not false-current)\n4. For daemon: call new getDaemonStatus() extracted from serve.ts\n5. Compute overall: healthy = (errors === 0)\n\n**Extract getDaemonStatus() from serve.ts**\nCurrently statusServer() in serve.ts mixes data-gathering with output. Extract into shared function in pid-utils.ts or new daemon-status.ts. Include projects array to avoid regressing serve status output. readPort() throws on missing/invalid port file — wrap in try/catch returning null.\n\n**Fix getSetupStatus staleness false-positive**\nIn setup.ts lines 1106 and 1109, status falls back to \"current\" when hash can't be checked. Change to \"unknown\". Update SetupStatus.agentsMd.status type to include \"unknown\" (line 965). Update text renderer in setup.ts.\n\n**Extract setup status logic to avoid CLI coupling**\nExtract pure status-gathering logic into src/parser/setup-status.ts. CLI command keeps formatter, calls extracted function. Avoids doctor.ts depending on CLI command module.\n\n**CLI layer: src/cli/commands/doctor.ts (new)**\nThin wrapper: getGitRoot() -> getDoctorReport(gitRoot) -> output(report, formatDoctorReport) -> exit based on report.overall.healthy.\nRegistration: Add to src/cli/commands/index.ts and wire in src/cli/index.ts.\n\n**Files to create/modify:**\n- src/parser/doctor.ts — NEW getDoctorReport() library function\n- src/cli/commands/doctor.ts — NEW CLI command wrapper\n- src/parser/setup-status.ts — NEW extracted getSetupStatus()/SetupStatus\n- src/cli/commands/setup.ts — Refactor to call extracted getSetupStatus(); fix staleness type\n- src/cli/commands/serve.ts — Extract getDaemonStatus() from statusServer()\n- src/cli/pid-utils.ts — Or put getDaemonStatus() here alongside PidFileManager\n- src/cli/commands/index.ts — Add export\n- src/cli/index.ts — Wire registration\n\n**Existing code to reuse:**\n- getShadowStatus() — src/parser/shadow.ts:267\n- PidFileManager — src/cli/pid-utils.ts:18\n- output() — src/cli/output.ts\n- EXIT_CODES — src/cli/exit-codes.ts\n- getGitRoot() — src/parser/shadow.ts",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHWJ2G70479CVV6AHSH2F6F4",
        "created_at": "2026-02-20T03:39:08.384Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implementation complete. Changes:\n\n1. **src/parser/doctor.ts (NEW)** - Library layer with getDoctorReport() function\n   - DoctorReport type with shadow, setup, daemon, and overall sections\n   - Each check includes severity (ok/warning/error), message, and guidance\n   - AC annotations for all 14 acceptance criteria\n\n2. **src/parser/daemon-status.ts (NEW)** - Extracted daemon status checking\n   - getDaemonStatus() probes PID file, verifies process, checks health endpoint\n   - AC: ac-daemon-running, ac-daemon-not-running, ac-daemon-unreachable\n\n3. **src/parser/setup-status.ts (NEW)** - Extracted setup status checking\n   - getSetupStatus() checks hooks, skills, agents.md, seeding\n   - AC: ac-setup-agent-hooks, ac-setup-skills-agents-md, ac-staleness-unknown\n\n4. **src/cli/commands/doctor.ts (NEW)** - CLI command wrapper\n   - Formats report for human-readable output\n   - Supports --json flag for JSON output (AC-12)\n   - Exit code 0 when healthy, 1 when errors (AC-13, AC-14)\n\n5. **src/cli/commands/setup.ts (MODIFIED)**\n   - Added 'unknown' to agentsMd.status type (AC-11)\n   - Fixed false-positive: now returns 'unknown' instead of 'current' when hash cannot be computed\n   - Updated status display to handle 'unknown' status\n\n6. **src/cli/commands/index.ts** - Added registerDoctorCommand export\n7. **src/cli/index.ts** - Wired registerDoctorCommand registration\n\n8. **tests/parser/doctor.test.ts (NEW)** - 26 tests covering all 14 ACs\n   - Tests for git repo check (AC-1)\n   - Tests for not initialized (AC-2)\n   - Tests for shadow healthy (AC-3)\n   - Tests for setup hooks (AC-4) and skills/agents.md (AC-5)\n   - Tests for daemon running (AC-6), unreachable (AC-7), not running (AC-8)\n   - Tests for overall verdict (AC-9)\n   - Tests for partial init (AC-10) and staleness unknown (AC-11)\n   - Tests for JSON output (AC-12) and exit codes (AC-13, AC-14)\n\nAll 2939 tests pass (1 pre-existing failure in daemon-executable.test.ts unrelated).",
        "supersedes": null
      },
