    "title": "Bump @agentclientprotocol/sdk to ^0.14.0",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "Bump the ACP SDK version to match what claude-agent-acp@0.18.0 depends on (0.14.1).\n\n## Current state\n\n- kynetic-spec pins @agentclientprotocol/sdk at ^0.13.0 (devDependency, types-only)\n- claude-agent-acp@0.18.0 depends on @agentclientprotocol/sdk@0.14.1\n\n## Risk: Very Low\n\nThe SDK is types-only (devDependency, erased at runtime). All 21 imported types in src/acp/types.ts still exist in 0.14.1 with compatible shapes. Changes between versions are strictly additive:\n- SessionUpdate union gets new \"usage_update\" variant (ignored by our code)\n- PromptResponse gets optional usage field (we only read stopReason)\n- RequestId changes bigint->number (we don't import this type)\n- No types removed\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Update package.json: \"@agentclientprotocol/sdk\": \"^0.14.0\"\n2. npm install\n3. tsc --noEmit to verify compilation\n4. Run test suite",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #451. Bumped @agentclientprotocol/sdk from ^0.13.0 to ^0.14.0. Types-only devDependency with zero breaking changes. All CI checks passed, 3105 tests green.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 3,
    "tags": [
      "acp-migration"
    ],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-20T19:54:24.467Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-23T00:08:31.298Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-23T00:24:30.815Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHYAV0VBJ0EQNFTQN3W30HC0",
        "created_at": "2026-02-20T20:11:12.107Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "ACP SDK type diff analysis (0.13.0 → 0.14.1):\n\nOf 23 imported types: 19 identical, 2 additive, 2 have bigint→number on unused fields. Zero breaking changes for our code.\n\nNew types available after bump:\n- Usage: token counts (input, output, cached, thought, total)\n- UsageUpdate: context window size/used + Cost\n- Cost: cumulative session cost (amount + currency)\n\nThese power the new usage_update SessionUpdate variant and PromptResponse.usage field. Could surface in ralph session stats later (token usage per iteration, cumulative cost). Not needed for migration.\n\nAlso stabilized: SessionConfigOption types (were experimental). We don't use these.",
        "supersedes": null
