  {
    "_ulid": "01KHY9WVP1ZSW3CZA2TNYEAYNT",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Spike: Validate claude-agent-acp 0.18.0 runtime compatibility",
    "type": "spike",
    "description": "Cannot determine from code analysis alone whether the _meta.claudeCode.* fields survive the MCP-to-native-tools migration in PR #316. Needs runtime testing.\n\n## Context\n\nPR zed-industries/claude-agent-acp#316 (merged 2026-02-18) removed the custom MCP server that proxied tools and switched to Claude Code's built-in tools. This changes how tool calls flow internally, which could affect the _meta structure on SessionUpdate events.\n\n## What to validate\n\n1. Install claude-agent-acp@0.18.0 globally\n2. Run a ralph loop (single iteration, simple task) and capture events.jsonl\n3. Check events for these critical fields:\n\n_meta.claudeCode.toolName:\n- Still present on tool_call and tool_call_update events?\n- Value is bare name (\"Bash\") not MCP-prefixed (\"mcp__acp__Bash\")?\n- Our normalizeTool() already strips prefixes, so prefix change is safe — but field absence is NOT safe.\n\n_meta.claudeCode.toolResponse:\n- Still present on tool completion events?\n- Still has stdout/stderr structure?\n- Or has it moved to rawOutput / _meta.terminal_output.data?\n\n--dangerously-skip-permissions:\n- Still accepted as a CLI flag?\n- Still skips permission prompts?\n\nsession/request_permission:\n- Still sends option.kind = \"allow_always\" / \"allow_once\"?\n- Still sends option.optionId field?\n\n4. Check the 0.14.0, 0.15.0, 0.16.0, 0.17.0 changelogs for any other breaking changes between our 0.13.2 and target 0.18.0.\n\n## Fallback paths already in our code\n\nextractToolName() has 4-level fallback: _meta.claudeCode.toolName -> _meta.toolName -> name -> title\nextractToolOutput() has 3-level fallback: rawOutput -> _meta.claudeCode.toolResponse -> output\n\nIf fields moved but data is still present somewhere in the update, our fallbacks may already handle it. The spike should confirm.\n\n## Outcome\n\nDocument which fields changed (if any) and whether our existing fallback chains handle them. If changes needed, create follow-up tasks with specific field mapping updates.",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Spike validated ACP 0.18.0 runtime compatibility against real ralph session (16 iterations, 27k events). All critical fields present and working. No code changes needed — existing fallback chains handle everything correctly. Only untested item is permission event fields (low risk, requires non-yolo run).",
    "depends_on": [
      "@01KHY9VV",
      "@01KHY9W8"
    ],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 2,
    "tags": [
      "acp-migration"
    ],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-20T19:54:43.776Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-23T22:25:27.378Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-23T22:25:56.908Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHYA7W5JQCRRAWQA2GH4AANK",
        "created_at": "2026-02-20T20:00:44.722Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Automation status set to manual_only: Spikes require interactive runtime testing and human judgment on outcomes",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KHYAGE5GP1A7Q9GWHBYR58Z7",
        "created_at": "2026-02-20T20:05:25.298Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Additional validation items discovered from changelog review (v0.13.2 → v0.18.0):\n\n1. rawOutput field (v0.14.0): tool_call_update now includes rawOutput. Our extractToolOutput() already checks rawOutput as priority 1 — verify this works correctly with real adapter output.\n\n2. config_option_update events (v0.18.0): New SessionUpdate discriminator value. Our translator's default case returns null for unknown types — should be safe, but verify no crash.\n\n3. current_mode_update events (v0.14.0): Plan mode transitions now emit notifications. Verify our event translator handles these gracefully (should fall through to null).\n\n4. Edit tool diff content blocks (v0.18.0): Edit results now include {type: \"diff\"} content blocks. Verify extractToolOutput() still extracts output correctly.\n\n5. Bash code fence language (v0.18.0): Changed from ```sh to ```console in formatted output. Check if any ralph rendering or pattern matching depends on this.\n\n6. disallowedTools merge fix (v0.16.0/v0.18.0): User-provided disallowedTools no longer silently dropped. We don't currently pass disallowedTools, but good to know.\n\n7. configOptions in NewSessionResponse (v0.18.0): Session creation response now has configOptions array. Verify our newSession() handling doesn't choke on extra fields.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJ69QG0MM0R2NYYW0GC82ZMT",
        "created_at": "2026-02-23T22:25:43.444Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "[SPIKE COMPLETE] ACP 0.18.0 runtime validation against ralph session 01KJ4VNM972YKRADFPC84B55RY (16 iterations, 27k events).\n\n## Core Fields — All Present and Working\n\n- _meta.claudeCode.toolName: Present on all 1,733 tool_call events. Always bare names (Bash, Read, Edit, etc.) — no MCP prefix.\n- _meta.claudeCode.toolResponse: Present on 1,690 completion events. Tool-specific structure intact (stdout/stderr for Bash, content/filenames for Grep, etc.).\n- rawOutput: Present on all 1,733 completion events as string. extractToolOutput() hits this at priority 1.\n- --dangerously-skip-permissions: Working — zero permission events in session (all auto-approved).\n\n## New Event Types (all handled gracefully)\n\n- `plan` (128 events): Unknown to translator, returns null. No crash.\n- `available_commands_update` (17 events): Same — returns null.\n- `null` updates (32 events): Handled gracefully.\n- `config_option_update`, `current_mode_update`: NOT observed in this session.\n\n## Phased Tool Call Model (ACP 0.14+)\n\n- tool_call events: Have kind, status:\"pending\", rawInput (always empty {}). Our code falls through rawInput to input field correctly.\n- tool_call_update streaming: Have content array with {type:\"content\"} blocks, no rawOutput.\n- tool_call_update completion: Have rawOutput (string), status, _meta.claudeCode.toolResponse.\n- Already handled by existing tool_call/tool_call_update logic in events.ts.\n\n## Edit Tool Diff Blocks\n\n- Edit completions use {type:\"diff\", path, oldText, newText} content blocks.\n- No impact: extractToolOutput() hits rawOutput first, diff blocks are in content array.\n\n## Bash Code Fence Language\n\n- Not applicable: rawOutput is plain string, no SDK-injected fences.\n\n## Fallback Chain Status\n\n- extractToolName(): Level 1 (_meta.claudeCode.toolName) always hits.\n- extractToolOutput(): Level 1 (rawOutput) hits on completions. Level 2 (toolResponse) present as backup.\n\n## Untested\n\n- Permission event field structure (option.kind, optionId): Session used yolo mode, so no permission events were generated. Would need a non-yolo run to verify. Low risk — the handleRequest code already uses these fields and the session ran successfully.\n\n## Verdict\n\nNo code changes needed. Existing fallback chains handle ACP 0.18.0 correctly.",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "automation": "manual_only",
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
  },
  {
    "_ulid": "01KHY9XF0Y160G7K8F4K0YVFM4",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Spike: Audit mock completeness vs real adapter behavior",
    "type": "spike",
    "description": "The ACP test mock (tests/mocks/acp-mock.js) is minimal and may not reflect real adapter behavior after the upgrade. Needs assessment.\n\n## Current mock limitations\n\n1. Only emits agent_message_chunk — never sends tool_call, tool_call_update, agent_thought_chunk events\n2. No empty-string finalization signal (real Claude Code sends content.text === \"\" to signal stream end)\n3. Permission handling only tested indirectly via mock's mirrored logic\n4. No _meta.claudeCode.* fields in emitted events (tool name/output extraction untested at integration level)\n5. SessionUpdate discriminator values hardcoded as strings, not validated against SDK types\n\n## What to investigate\n\n1. Run a real ralph session and capture events.jsonl\n2. Compare the real SessionUpdate structures against what the mock emits\n3. Identify gaps: which real event patterns are NOT covered by mock or unit tests?\n4. Specifically check:\n   - tool_call events: do they have _meta.claudeCode.toolName in the real adapter?\n   - tool_call_update events: do they have rawOutput or _meta.claudeCode.toolResponse?\n   - Does the real adapter send duplicate tool_call events (the \"alreadyCached\" pattern from PR #316)?\n   - Are there new SessionUpdate variants (e.g. usage_update) that the translator should handle?\n\n## Outcome\n\nEither:\n- The mock is sufficient and unit tests in ralph.test.ts cover the gaps (likely)\n- Or create tasks to extend the mock and/or add integration test scenarios\n\n## Note\n\nThis can be combined with the runtime compatibility spike if convenient — both require running a real ralph session. But the focus here is on test coverage, not adapter compatibility.",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "pending",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "depends_on": [
      "@01KHY9WV"
    ],
