    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Skip kspec-agents.md regeneration when content unchanged",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "kspec agents generate currently always updates the timestamp in kspec-agents.md even when no actual content has changed. This creates unnecessary git diffs. Should compare the generated content (excluding the timestamp comment) against the existing file and skip writing if identical. The hash file (.kspec-agents-hash) already tracks meta hash for staleness — if the meta hash matches, the file content is the same and generation can be skipped entirely with a 'kspec-agents.md is already up to date' message.",
    "spec_ref": "@agent-instruction-gen",
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #438. agents generate now checks stored meta hash before writing — skips with 'already up to date' when content unchanged. 3 tests for ac-6.",
