  {
    "_ulid": "01KJ315WHBK8887TZQXY8HG9DH",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Spike: Design interactive triage system with persistent metadata",
    "type": "task",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Spike complete. Plan imported with 6 specs and 6 tasks. Dependencies set.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 2,
    "tags": [
      "spike",
      "design",
      "inbox",
      "triage"
    ],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-22T15:58:34.538Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-22T20:16:48.921Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-22T20:16:53.170Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJ3168YTVCBZ7EPD5W213YPA",
        "created_at": "2026-02-22T15:58:47.258Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Spike to explore design space and produce spec-plan for interactive triage system.\n\n## Problem\nInbox triage is currently agent-driven and ephemeral. Triage decisions (reasoning, evidence, actions, user decisions) are lost between sessions. No way for users to interactively review/override agent triage. No way for subsequent agents to act on prior triage work reliably.\n\n## Design Space\n\n### 1. Triage Metadata on Inbox Items\nAdd structured fields: triage_status, triage_reasoning, triage_evidence, triage_action, user_decision, spec_gap flag, automation_eligible flag. Key question: extend InboxItem schema or separate TriageRecord?\n\n### 2. Interactive Triage UI (Web UI via Daemon)\nPer-category triage mode with one-by-one item presentation. Shows description, agent reasoning, evidence, recommended action. User chooses from options or overrides. Free-form input for reasoning. Next/previous navigation. Writes through daemon API to shadow branch.\n\n### 3. Agent Handoff Export\nContext-rich export of triage decisions for fresh agent sessions. Include full item context, triage metadata, user decision, relevant refs. Format must give new agents enough context to act without re-researching. Possibly: kspec inbox export --triaged\n\n### 4. Daemon API Extensions\nGET/PUT /api/inbox/:ref/triage, filtering by triage_status, bulk updates.\n\n## Key Questions\n- Schema: inline on inbox items or separate triage records?\n- History: version triage decisions (agent triages, user overrides)?\n- Workflow: integrate with existing /triage skill?\n- Export: what format maximizes agent effectiveness?\n\n## References\n- Triage skill: .claude/skills/triage/\n- Inbox schema: src/schema/inbox.ts  \n- Daemon API: packages/daemon/src/\n- Web UI inbox: packages/web-ui/src/routes/inbox/\n- Triage report artifact: .kspec/artifacts/triage-report-2026-02-22.html (example of current ephemeral output)",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
  },
