    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #446. Artifacts directory convention implemented: init/setup/repair create .kspec/artifacts/, doctor health check, .gitignore exclusion, 6 tests. Codex review noted: spec wording re .gitkeep should be updated (intentionally skipped since dir is gitignored), setup hardcodes .kspec path (low-risk), repair doesn't ensure .gitignore for legacy branches.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 3,
    "tags": [
      "spec",
      "dx",
      "convention"
    ],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-22T15:58:53.742Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-22T17:47:04.173Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-22T18:30:32.817Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJ316VA1XV93XEQH15S54FN5",
        "created_at": "2026-02-22T15:59:06.049Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Directory created and gitignored. Remaining work is spec + documentation.\n\n## Done\n- Created .kspec/artifacts/ directory\n- Added .kspec/.gitignore to exclude artifacts/ from shadow branch commits\n- Moved first artifact (triage-report-2026-02-22.html) there\n\n## Remaining (needs spec)\n- Spec the convention: what goes in artifacts, naming patterns, lifecycle\n- Add to kspec setup: create artifacts/ dir during init\n- Document in AGENTS.md or template sections: when to use artifacts/ vs other locations\n- Consider: kspec artifacts list, kspec artifacts clean --older-than Nd\n- Consider: should agents auto-name artifacts with date prefix? (current: triage-report-2026-02-22.html)\n- Add to doctor command: check artifacts/ exists\n\n## Design Questions\n- Should artifacts be purely ephemeral or optionally tracked?\n- Naming convention: <type>-<date>.ext? <type>-<session-id>.ext?\n- Max size/age policy?\n- Should kspec generate commands output to artifacts/ by default?",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJ37C8HXX2K25VFZNCKSBWJN",
        "created_at": "2026-02-22T17:46:54.909Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Spec created: @artifacts-directory with 8 ACs covering init, setup, doctor, repair, gitignore, naming convention, and empty dir persistence. Review identified key gaps: .gitkeep for empty dir survival, name collision handling, shadow repair behavior, and AC redundancy — all addressed in final spec. Implementation scope: modify init (shadow.ts), setup pipeline, doctor checks, and shadow repair to create/check .kspec/artifacts/ with .gitkeep.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJ37TGWDEGXT1KHDRJNNYQVV",
        "created_at": "2026-02-22T17:54:42.189Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Implementation complete for 6 of 8 ACs:\n\n- ac-init-creates: initializeShadow() creates artifacts/ dir (shadow.ts ~line 1708)\n- ac-gitignore-entry: .gitignore with artifacts/ written during init (shadow.ts ~line 1710)\n- ac-commits-exclude: Covered by gitignore — tested that git add -A doesn't stage artifacts\n- ac-setup-ensures: runSetupPipeline() creates artifacts/ if missing (setup.ts ~line 1542)\n- ac-doctor-checks: buildShadowSection() checks artifactsDirExists (doctor.ts ~line 257)\n- ac-repair-recreates: repairShadow() creates artifacts/ after worktree rebuild (shadow.ts ~line 1818)\n\nConvention-only ACs (no code enforcement):\n- ac-naming-convention: Documented pattern type-YYYY-MM-DD.ext — agents follow by reading spec\n- ac-empty-dir-persistence: Handled by init/setup/repair creating the dir (not via .gitkeep since gitignore excludes artifacts/)\n\nTests added: 6 new tests across shadow.test.ts and doctor.test.ts. All 112+29 pass.",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
