        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Spec gap: plugin marketplace registration is incomplete.\n\n## Problem\nkspec setup registers a 'directory' source marketplace but the plugin/ dir only has .claude-plugin/plugin.json (single plugin manifest). Claude Code expects .claude-plugin/marketplace.json (marketplace listing format) for directory sources. Warning: 'Failed to load marketplace kspec-plugins: marketplace.json not found'.\n\n## What Exists\n- plugin/.claude-plugin/plugin.json - single plugin manifest (name, version, description)\n- plugin/skills/help/SKILL.md - one core skill\n- src/lib/claude-plugin-registry.ts - registers marketplace in known_marketplaces.json\n- Build step populates plugin/ from templates/skills/\n\n## What's Missing\n1. marketplace.json generation: build step should produce .claude-plugin/marketplace.json wrapping the kspec plugin entry in the marketplace plugins array format\n2. Validate against official marketplace schema (see ~/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/claude-plugins-official/.claude-plugin/marketplace.json for reference format)\n3. Spec coverage: review @plugin-rendering and @core-skill-installation specs for marketplace.json AC gaps\n4. Test: verify claude doctor shows no plugin errors after setup\n\n## Reference\n- Fix commit: 47453817 (directory source type fix)\n- Official marketplace format: { name, description, owner, plugins: [{ name, description, version, source, ... }] }\n- PR #444 shipped the plugin system but missed marketplace.json requirement",
        "supersedes": null
