    "description": "Doctor tests (tests/parser/doctor.test.ts) have been reported as failing intermittently by agents during ralph loop sessions. The 29-test suite passes consistently in isolation but has been observed failing during automated runs.\n\nInvestigation needed:\n- Reproduce the flaky failure (run test suite in loop or under load)\n- Check for timing/race conditions (daemon status checks, file system operations)\n- Check for test isolation issues (shared state between tests, temp dir cleanup)\n- Review recent ralph logs or session notes for specific error messages\n- Determine if related to daemon health check timeouts or mock reliability\n\nThe doctor test covers: shadow health, setup status, daemon running/unreachable/not-running, overall verdict, JSON output, exit codes. Any of these could have timing sensitivity.",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #456. Root cause: getDaemonStatus() checks global PID file, not per-project. Fix: added vi.spyOn mocking in 3 daemon tests to isolate from host environment. Previous SHOULD-FIX (ac-daemon-running not testing running state) addressed. All 3168 tests pass.",
