    "title": "Audit test suite and plan migration from static analysis to behavioral tests",
    "type": "spike",
    "description": "The test suite relies heavily on static analysis patterns — reading source files and checking for string patterns (e.g. expect(content).toContain(...)). This approach cannot catch runtime bugs and breaks on refactors (e.g. end-loop.test.ts had regex pattern tests that could not detect the false-positive bug that caused a real ralph loop exit).\n\nDeep dive:\n1) Inventory ALL test files repo-wide and categorize by test approach (static analysis vs behavioral vs E2E).\n2) Identify which static-only tests have the highest risk of missing real bugs.\n3) Design a migration plan — options include: unit tests that import functions directly, integration tests with fixtures, CLI behavioral tests, or Playwright E2E tests.\n4) Create follow-up tasks for the actual migration work.\n\nKnown areas with static analysis tests:\n- Daemon tests (tests/daemon-*.test.ts)\n- Ralph end-loop tests (tests/ralph/end-loop.test.ts) — session close handlers, marker removal\n- Likely others across the test suite\n\nThe pattern to eliminate: reading source with fs.readFile then expect(content).toContain(...)",
