        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Session audit 01KJ8Z3Q identified additional static analysis tests to include: (1) end-loop.test.ts lines 255-372 — 5 tests reading ralph.ts source for string patterns (ac-detect, session close handlers, ac-remove-markers), (2) session-budget-integration.test.ts lines 295-339 — marker code removal tests reading ralph.ts source. Both files already have behavioral equivalents alongside the static ones, so migration = delete static tests after confirming behavioral coverage.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJBK313W12Q9TCXPF8X620QH",
        "created_at": "2026-02-25T23:45:30.749Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "AUDIT COMPLETE — Inventory of static analysis tests across the repo:\n\n**7 files with static analysis patterns, ~59 total tests.**\n\nHIGH RISK (P1):\n- daemon-server.test.ts: ~13 tests read packages/daemon/src/server.ts and check string patterns for port, hostname, health, CORS, signals, WebSocket. Zero runtime verification of daemon behavior.\n- ralph/end-loop.test.ts lines 254-372: 8 tests read src/cli/commands/ralph.ts checking session state detection, signal handlers, session close paths, marker removal. Already known to miss real bugs (false-positive end-loop exit bug).\n\nMEDIUM RISK (P2):\n- ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts lines 293-339: 13 tests checking marker code removal (26 patterns). Absence tests.\n- normalize-ref-input.test.ts lines 55-139: 8 tests doing lint-style anti-pattern detection on CLI commands and daemon routes.\n- skill-module-split.test.ts lines 18-69: 6 tests checking file existence and string patterns. Same file has good behavioral tests on lines 74-120.\n- web-ui-shared-types.test.ts: 5 tests checking re-export patterns in type files.\n\nLOW RISK (P3):\n- package-distribution.test.ts: 6 tests checking template file content patterns.\n\nMIGRATION APPROACHES:\n1. daemon-server → E2E Playwright tests hitting actual endpoints\n2. ralph end-loop/session-budget → Import functions directly, unit test logic\n3. normalize-ref-input → ESLint custom rule or keep as lint-like\n4. skill-module-split → Convert to import-based checks (already partially done)\n5. web-ui-shared-types → TypeScript import verification\n6. package-distribution → npm pack --dry-run for realistic verification\n\n~40+ other files use readFile legitimately (reading test output, YAML fixtures, etc.)",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
