    "slugs": [
      "task-fix-sidebar-nav-links"
    ],
    "title": "Fix web UI sidebar navigation links not clickable",
    "type": "bug",
    "description": "SidebarMenuButton renders a <button> element, not an <a>. When Sidebar.svelte passes href, the href lands on a button (which browsers ignore). Result: Dashboard, Tasks, Items, Inbox, Triage links are all dead — only Observations works because it uses onclick with goto(). Fix: either use the child snippet pattern to render an <a> tag, or add onclick handlers with goto() like Observations does. Also add /triage to the spaRoutes array in packages/daemon/src/server.ts line 338 so the daemon serves index.html for the triage route.",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #457. Fixed sidebar nav links by using shadcn-svelte child snippet pattern to render <a> elements instead of dead <button> elements. Added /triage to daemon SPA fallback routes. User manually verified links work and triage page renders.",
