    "description": "Configure CI to only run the test suite when files that affect test outcomes are changed. Use GitHub Actions path filters to skip tests for documentation-only, skill-only, or other non-code changes.\n\nApproach: Define paths that trigger tests (src/**, tests/**, packages/**, package.json, etc.) rather than paths that skip tests. This is safer — new code paths get tested by default.\n\nExamples of changes that should skip tests:\n- .claude/skills/**\n- docs/**\n- templates/agents-sections/**\n- *.md (except possibly SKILL.md files that get loaded at runtime — evaluate)\n- .kspec/**\n\nConsider: GitHub Actions path filtering with paths/paths-ignore on the test job.",
