    "type": "task",
    "description": "In ralph.ts:1573-1579, the streaming update event handler fires appendEvent() without await (fire-and-forget). The iteration variable is captured by closure reference, not by value. By the time the async callback executes, iteration has already been incremented in the for loop — so hundreds of tool_call events get tagged with the wrong iteration number. Fix: snapshot iteration into a const before the closure. One-line fix.",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #485. Handles phased tool call events from ACP SDK 0.14+: translator emits summaries when rawInput arrives late, deduplication in session display/stats/search. 7 new tests, all CI green.",
    "depends_on": [],
