        "content": "Completed with --skip-review: Spike complete. Investigated session scoping approach for kspec, including:\n- Cross-harness env var research (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Gemini CLI)\n- Current session/ralph/hook architecture analysis\n- Design of session-scoped budget enforcement replacing marker files + bash hooks\n- Dual review (internal + Codex) with all MUST-FIX findings addressed\n\nDeliverables:\n- Plan @plan-session-scoping-for-kspec imported with 6 specs, 10 tasks\n- Dependencies set between tasks\n- Specs have traits: @trait-json-output, @trait-semantic-exit-codes, @trait-error-guidance\n- Key design decisions: budget on local filesystem (not shadow branch), single-writer guarantee, cooperative enforcement, end-loop migrated to session state, sessions always closed",
