    "title": "Fix: detectTaskCompleteCommand should match task submit",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "detectTaskCompleteCommand() in ralph.ts (~line 229) only matches 'kspec task complete' but not 'kspec task submit'. When the agent submits a task (pending_review), ralph never detects it, never writes the marker file, and the agent keeps picking up new tasks — bypassing --max-tasks. Fix: add 'submit' to the detection pattern. Also update getIterationStats() to count pending_review tasks toward the limit.",
    "spec_ref": "@ralph-task-limit",
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
