    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Free budget for no-op task completions in ralph loop",
    "type": "spike",
    "description": "When a task is completed as 'already implemented' (--skip-review) during a ralph loop iteration, it counts against --max-tasks budget. This wastes iterations. Proposed approach: track task starts and completes per iteration; if a complete happens without a corresponding start after iteration reset, treat it as free (don't count against budget). Needs design review for edge cases around fix cycles and skip-review completions.",
