    "title": "Document N/A trait AC annotation format in testing convention",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "When a trait AC doesn't apply to a spec, the correct annotation format is:\n`// AC: @trait-slug ac-N N/A — reason`\n\nNot prose comments like `// @trait-slug ac-N: N/A — reason` or bullet lists in file headers.\n\nThis came up in PR #503 where Codex flagged N/A trait ACs as MUST-FIX because they used prose instead of the // AC: prefix. The convention should be documented in the testing convention (templates/agents-sections/) so agents get it right the first time.\n\nUpdate:\n- templates/agents-sections/ testing section to include N/A annotation format\n- Regenerate kspec-agents.md after",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #520. Documented N/A trait AC annotation format in templates/agents-sections/05-commit-convention.md and regenerated kspec-agents.md. Prior SHOULD-FIX about hardcoded // AC: prefix was addressed. All CI passed.",
