  {
    "_ulid": "01KJ8T2N7APYPYDEHM2WVP7ZTX",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Fix test failures when running inside ralph loop (env pollution)",
    "type": "bug",
    "description": "4 tests fail when vitest runs inside a ralph loop because ralph sets KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION and KSPEC_SESSION_ID on process.env, and child processes inherit them.",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #509. Fixed env pollution when vitest runs inside ralph loop by stripping KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION and KSPEC_SESSION_ID from child process env in kspec() test helper and ralph.test.ts direct spawnSync call. All 3513 tests pass. Codex review clean.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 1,
    "tags": [
      "testing",
      "ralph"
    ],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-24T21:49:55.305Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-24T22:01:48.978Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-24T22:13:36.448Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJ8T35W8Q3AJRFJD4DJBARNM",
        "created_at": "2026-02-24T21:50:12.360Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "## Failing Tests (4 total, 3 files)\n\n### 1-2. session-create.test.ts — JSON parse errors (lines 774, 860)\nTests: 'should return error as JSON when --json is active and validation fails' and 'should include guidance in JSON error object'\n- Run: kspec session create --budget abc --json (expectFail)\n- Then: JSON.parse(result.stderr)\n- Fails because: KSPEC_SESSION_ID is set in env (inherited from ralph), pointing to ralph's session. session create validates this env var (src/cli/commands/session.ts:2080-2088) and calls warn() which writes '⚠ Current KSPEC_SESSION_ID (...) is invalid: ...' to stderr BEFORE the JSON error object. JSON.parse fails on the warning prefix.\n\n### 3. session-create.test.ts — env injection method (line 740)\nTest: 'should inject via .env when OpenCode detected'\n- Expects injection.method === 'opencode_dotenv' but gets 'fallback'\n- Ralph env vars interfere with harness detection logic\n\n### 4. ralph.test.ts — KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION inheritance (line 612)\nTest: 'KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION is not inherited by non-ralph child processes'\n- Spawns child with { ...process.env } expecting KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION absent\n- Running inside ralph means process.env.KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION IS set\n- Gets '01KJ8MK...' instead of null\n\n### 5. session-budget-integration.test.ts (intermittent)\nTest: 'should clean up budget.json after normal exit'\n- Similar env pollution from ralph session vars\n\n## Root Cause\nRalph sets KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION and KSPEC_SESSION_ID on process.env. The kspec() test helper in tests/helpers/cli.ts uses spawnSync which inherits process.env. Tests that expect clean env get ralph's vars instead.\n\n## Fix Approach\nIn tests/helpers/cli.ts, the kspec() helper should strip ralph-specific env vars (KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION, KSPEC_SESSION_ID) from the spawned process env by default. Tests that explicitly need these vars already pass them via the env option.\n\nSpecifically in cli.ts around the spawnSync call: build the child env from process.env but delete KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION and KSPEC_SESSION_ID unless the test explicitly provides them via opts.env.\n\nThe ralph.test.ts line 607 also needs fixing: it uses { ...process.env } directly in its own spawnSync (not via the helper), so it needs the same treatment.\n\n## Verification\nRun tests both standalone (npx vitest run) and inside ralph loop to confirm both pass.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJ8TS8J778Q2G2PJ4S7VZRGA",
        "created_at": "2026-02-24T22:02:16.007Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Iteration 5 did not work on this task — focused on @implement-session-start-dependency-display (PR #508) instead. The diagnosis and fix approach in the previous note are thorough and ready to implement. Next iteration should pick this up: strip KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION and KSPEC_SESSION_ID from child env in tests/helpers/cli.ts spawnSync, and fix ralph.test.ts line 607.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJ8TZTR93MC3PAT139KDE0Y3",
        "created_at": "2026-02-24T22:05:51.241Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Fixed env pollution by stripping KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION and KSPEC_SESSION_ID from child process env in two places: (1) tests/helpers/cli.ts kspec() helper — builds cleanEnv from process.env with ralph vars deleted unless explicitly passed via opts.env, (2) tests/ralph.test.ts line 607 — direct spawnSync call now strips ralph vars to simulate non-ralph child. All 3513 tests pass including the 4 previously-failing ones in session-create.test.ts, ralph.test.ts, and session-budget-integration.test.ts.",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
    "automation": "eligible",
    "_sourceFile": "/workspace/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml"
  },
  {
    "_ulid": "01KJ8WSBNJJ21TNJVQVN66D8KS",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Review skills should always dig for task/spec context, never skip AC checks",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "PR reviewers (codex, pr-review, local-review) should never skip AC/spec validation just because a PR lacks a Task trailer. They should dig deeper: check commit messages for Task:/Spec: trailers, search recent tasks matching PR scope, check AC annotations in changed files, and validate against found specs. Currently codex SKILL.md line 128 explicitly says to skip AC checks when no trailer exists. pr-review requires a task ref as a hard gate. Both need updating to always pursue spec context.",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #511. Updated 4 skill files (codex, pr-review, local-review, review template) with dig-deeper spec context discovery pattern. Reviewers now check commit trailers, task list search, and AC annotations before falling back to pure code review. All codex review findings addressed.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 1,
    "tags": [
      "review",
      "skills"
    ],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-24T22:37:16.338Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-24T22:45:45.844Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-24T23:02:18.028Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJ8WSSCFT27761HWH249M888",
        "created_at": "2026-02-24T22:37:30.383Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "## Problem\n\nCodex PR review said 'No PR Task trailer was present, so spec/trait AC coverage checks were skipped per instructions' on PR #510. This defeats the purpose of spec-first development — reviewers should always validate against specs.\n\n## Affected Skills\n\n### 1. .claude/skills/codex/SKILL.md (line 128)\nCurrent: 'If no Task trailer exists, proceed with pure code review (skip AC checks).'\nFix: Replace with instructions to dig deeper — check commit trailers, search tasks list, check AC annotations in changed files, then validate against found specs. Only fall back to pure code review if genuinely no spec coverage exists for the change.\n\n### 2. .claude/skills/pr-review/SKILL.md\nCurrent: Requires task ref as a hard validation gate ('Task reference required. Error immediately.')\nFix: Instead of erroring, dig for context the same way — commit trailers, task list search, AC annotations. The PR body trailer is a convenience, not a prerequisite.\n\n### 3. .claude/skills/local-review/SKILL.md\nCurrent: AC coverage checks are unconditional (good), but only when spec context is already known.\nFix: Add step to discover spec context if not explicitly provided — same dig-deeper pattern.\n\n## Dig-Deeper Pattern (apply to all three)\n\nWhen no Task trailer in PR body:\n1. Check commit messages for Task: or Spec: trailers\n2. Search recent tasks: kspec tasks list — match by title/description to PR scope\n3. Check if changed files have // AC: @spec-ref annotations pointing to specs\n4. If a spec is found, validate AC coverage identically to trailer-present case\n5. Only skip AC validation if genuinely no spec exists for the changed behavior\n\n## Principle\nReviewers should be investigators, not form-checkers. The absence of a trailer is a signal to look harder, not permission to skip validation.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJ8X5NM649HSJ5WFEEXN8YW9",
        "created_at": "2026-02-24T22:43:59.750Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Reset from in_progress to pending",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJ8XCHPFQZYHJ0AK4JC1P75M",
        "created_at": "2026-02-24T22:47:45.103Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Updated 4 skill files with dig-deeper spec context discovery pattern. Changes: (1) codex SKILL.md line 128 — replaced 'skip AC checks' with 5-step discovery process (commit trailers, task search, AC annotations, then validate if found). Also added discovery instruction to the simpler review subcommand prompt. (2) pr-review SKILL.md — removed hard error gate for missing task ref, replaced with discovery pattern that checks PR body, commit messages, diff annotations, and task list search. Now accepts PR numbers directly. (3) local-review SKILL.md — added Step 0: Discover Spec Context before the existing 8 steps. Falls back to code-quality-only review if no spec found. (4) templates/skills/review/SKILL.md — added Spec Context Discovery section as the base building block that all review skills reference. All 3513 tests pass (1 known flaky ralph timeout unrelated).",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
