  {
    "_ulid": "01KJ8XM5X8S04X7DSDP9TQQ9XR",
    "slugs": [
      "task-fix-flaky-ralph-budget-test"
    ],
    "title": "Fix flaky ralph session-budget-integration timeout test",
    "type": "bug",
    "description": "The test 'should clean up budget.json after normal exit (max-iterations reached)' in tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts times out intermittently. The spawnRalphUntil helper has a 25s safety timeout that races against ralph completing a full iteration with the mock agent. Under CI load or during ralph loop, this timeout fires before ralph finishes. Possible approaches: increase timeout, optimize mock agent response time, or restructure to test cleanup without spawning full ralph subprocess.",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #512. Fixed flaky ralph session-budget-integration test by isolating subprocess cwd to tempDir with clean git repo and .gitignore for sessions/. All CI checks passed, review thread resolved.",
    "depends_on": [],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 2,
    "tags": [
      "bug",
      "testing",
      "ralph"
    ],
    "vcs_refs": [],
    "created_at": "2026-02-24T22:51:55.176Z",
    "started_at": "2026-02-24T23:22:48.146Z",
    "completed_at": "2026-02-24T23:30:02.922Z",
    "notes": [
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJ8YPSVS98VXZ2F396JFT7Y7",
        "created_at": "2026-02-24T23:10:49.721Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Root cause: spawnRalphUntil and testSignalCleanup helpers used cwd: process.cwd() (real project root). When the real working tree had uncommitted changes, getWorkingTreeStatus() returned dirty, causing runWrapUpAgent() to spawn a wrap-up agent with a 2-minute timeout — well exceeding the test's 25s safety timeout. Fix: (1) Changed cwd to tempDir (in /tmp, outside any git repo), (2) Initialize a clean git repo in tempDir with initial commit so getWorkingTreeStatus() reliably returns clean, (3) This ensures isWrapUpNeeded() returns false and wrap-up is skipped. All 3513 tests pass.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJ8Z5K1MGBRFZ4J52M6XK5NA",
        "created_at": "2026-02-24T23:18:54.260Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: Existing MUST-FIX from chapel's review is not addressed in pushed code: Ralph writes sessions/ artifacts in tempDir before wrap-up runs, making the repo dirty again despite the initial commit. The local uncommitted fix (adding .gitignore for sessions/) looks correct but needs to be committed and pushed to the PR branch.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
