      {
        "_ulid": "01KJ923S3EFT5SFD6G0Z04HX8W",
        "created_at": "2026-02-25T00:10:20.655Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Bug: kspec item set --status accepts arbitrary strings (e.g. 'specified') that aren't valid enum values. The invalid value gets written to YAML, passes through the CLI layer unchecked, and then causes Zod validation failures on read — making the entire item invisible to all lookups until manually fixed. Fix: validate --status value against the Zod enum (implementation: not_started|in_progress|implemented|verified, maturity: draft|proposed|stable|deferred|deprecated) before writing. On invalid input, fail with a clear error listing valid values. Applies to both kspec item set --status and kspec item set --maturity if that exists. Also covers @maturity-states ac-reject-invalid.",
        "supersedes": null
      },
      {
        "_ulid": "01KJ96Q18B55492DY3NJXYV8V9",
        "created_at": "2026-02-25T01:30:45.899Z",
        "author": "@claude",
        "content": "Added enum validation for --status and --maturity flags in item set command. Validates against ImplementationStatusSchema.options and MaturitySchema.options before writing. On invalid input, fails with clear error listing valid values and exits with USAGE_ERROR code. 6 integration tests covering both @implementation-states ac-reject-invalid and @maturity-states ac-reject-invalid: invalid value rejection, no-write verification, and all valid values acceptance. All 3592 tests pass (2 known flaky ralph signal tests).",
        "supersedes": null
      }
    ],
    "todos": [],
