    "_ulid": "01KJ9ZJPKKHWSJZT2E289J9B1Z",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Fix removeAllListeners() in readStdinIfAvailable to use named handlers",
    "type": "bug",
    "description": "In src/cli/commands/session.ts, the readStdinIfAvailable() function (~line 1669-1696) calls process.stdin.removeAllListeners() in its timeout handler. This removes ALL stdin listeners, not just the ones this function added, which could break other code with stdin listeners.\n\nFix: Replace with named handler functions and use process.stdin.removeListener(event, handler) to only clean up the specific handlers this function registered.\n\nCurrent pattern:\n  process.stdin.removeAllListeners()\n\nShould be:\n  const onData = (chunk) => { ... };\n  const onEnd = () => { ... };\n  process.stdin.on('data', onData);\n  process.stdin.on('end', onEnd);\n  // In cleanup:\n  process.stdin.removeListener('data', onData);\n  process.stdin.removeListener('end', onEnd);",
    "spec_ref": null,
    "meta_ref": null,
    "plan_ref": null,
    "status": "completed",
    "blocked_by": [],
    "closed_reason": "Merged in PR #526. Replaced removeAllListeners() with named handlers + cleanup() pattern in readStdinIfAvailable() and readStdinFully() in item.ts. Static analysis test added to prevent regression. All CI passed.",
    "depends_on": [
      "@01KJ9ZBT"
    ],
    "context": [],
    "priority": 2,
    "tags": [
      "bug",
      "cli"
    ],
    "vcs_refs": [],
