  {
    "_ulid": "01KJA01BXDN6M8EFJNJT8JNJSZ",
    "slugs": [],
    "title": "Optimize gatherSessionContext to use single-pass task bucketing",
    "type": "task",
    "description": "gatherSessionContext() in session.ts (after refactor: session/context.ts) filters allTasks 14 times:\n- .filter(in_progress) for stats\n- .filter(needs_work) for stats\n- .filter(pending_review) for stats\n- getReadyTasks(allTasks) (full pass)\n- .filter(blocked) for stats\n- .filter(completed) for stats\n- .filter(in_progress || needs_work) for active tasks\n- .filter(pending_review) for review tasks\n- .filter(in_progress || needs_work) again for notes\n- .filter(pending_review) again for notes\n- .filter(completed && completed_at) for completed notes\n- getReadyTasks(allTasks) again\n- .filter(blocked) again\n- .filter(completed && completed_at) again\n\nReplace with a single pass that buckets tasks by status into a Map<status, LoadedTask[]>, then use the buckets for stats, summaries, and notes. getReadyTasks() result should be cached.\n\nDepends on: @01KJ9ZBT (session.ts refactor — do this after the split so you're editing the focused context.ts file)",
