    "description": "In gatherSessionContext(), the note limit calculation has a potential bug:\n\n  const noteLimitPerStatus = options.full ? limit : Math.ceil(limit / 3);\n\nIn full mode, noteLimitPerStatus = limit. Then 3 separate arrays are created (in_progress/needs_work notes, pending_review notes, completed notes), each with up to `limit` items. When concatenated (~line 673), the result can be up to 3 * limit total notes.\n\nOther sections in the same function respect `limit` as a hard cap (e.g., ready tasks, blocked tasks, completed tasks all use .slice(0, limit)).\n\nInvestigate: Is the 3x behavior intentional for full mode (more notes = more context)? Or should total notes be capped at `limit` across all statuses?\n\nIf it's a bug: apply .slice(0, limit) to the concatenated notes array. If intentional: add a comment explaining why notes get 3x the limit.",
