    "description": "CI already shards tests into 3 with `npx vitest run --shard=N/3`. Add npm scripts so developers can do the same locally for faster feedback:\n\nAdd to package.json scripts:\n  \"test:shard1\": \"vitest run --shard=1/3\",\n  \"test:shard2\": \"vitest run --shard=2/3\",\n  \"test:shard3\": \"vitest run --shard=3/3\"\n\nOr a single parameterized script:\n  \"test:shard\": \"vitest run --shard\"\n  Usage: npm run test:shard -- --shard=1/3\n\nAlso consider documenting this in the testing convention (kspec meta) so agents know they can run a subset of tests for faster iteration during development. Full suite is still required before PR.\n\nCurrent full suite time: ~150s. Each shard would be ~50s.",
